WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.070
How deep does this thing go?

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.070
Picture this: You’re sailing along the Grand
Line, minding your own business, just straight

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.070
up chilling.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.070
When suddenly, you spot it: An Ice Berg.[Show
Ice Berg the One Piece Character]

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.070
No, not Ice Berg the shipwright.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.070
This ice berg is no simple character.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.070
This is the ONE PIECE ICE BERG.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.070
Embedded inside its icy walls are the greatest
mysteries and theories of the series.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.070
So hop in the Polar Tang [Show Law’s submarine]
and let’s plumb the depths to find out how

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.070
far down the One Piece fandom goes.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.070
Come with us on our journey to explore the
wildest theories the internet has to offer.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.070
Toby Hook:

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.070
Let’s talk about One Piece Ice Berg.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.070
No NOT the character!

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.070
The ice berg that contains the greatest mysteries
and theories in one piece!

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.070
I’ve seen a lot of videos breaking down
icebergs for different topics, but as far

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.070
as I know none about One Piece.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.930
In case you don’t know, the ice berg video
format is a system of levels starting with

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:24.070
popular and mainstream theories &amp; mysteries
of a certain topic, the tip of the ice berg

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:30.320
everyone knows, and then moving deeper towards
the wildest and darkest theories the internet

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.769
has to offer.

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:33.160
Starting with Tier 1.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.160
**TIER 1**

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.320
**Crocodile was born a woman.**

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.290
Rising above the surface of the waters, we
have a couple tier 1 theories that you’ve

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.160
probably heard of before.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.550
Like the theory that Crocodile was assigned
female at birth.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.350
Sir Crocodile, the first Shichibukai that
Luffy took down, remains to this day one of

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.840
the fandom’s favorite villains in the entire
manga.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.553
His cunning plans, awesome sand powers, and
an unforgettable laugh [use Croc’s laugh

00:00:56.553 --> 00:01:01.250
sound here] make him stand high above more
dangerous foes, even if he was defeated by

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.230
a pre-timeskip Luffy.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:08.220
But the leader of Baroque Works - Mr. 0, if
you will - has a secret even more secret that

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.220
his own identity.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:14.680
Moreover, the knowledge of this secret is
known to one Emporio Ivankov, the ruler of

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.110
the Kamabakka Queendom.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.610
And just what secret would the holder of the
hormone fruit be privy to?

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:25.320
Well, that Crocodile was born biologically
female and then thanks to Ivankov’s powers,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.159
physically transitioned to become male.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:29.979
In other words, Crocodile is a trans man.

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:34.399
After all, Oda’s drawing of a young Crocodile
is gender ambiguous.

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:36.619
**Admirals vs. Monster Trio**

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:39.270
The Marines have three very strong military
forces.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.259
The Straw Hats have three very strong pirates.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:43.360
They will fight.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.450
Or so the story went before Akainu earned
a promotion and Aokiji went off to hang with

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.450
Blackbeard.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.370
However, that’s not going to stop fans from
speculating who the final matchups will be

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:57.939
when it comes time for the Straw Hats to take
on the strongest Marine powers.

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:00.219
Luffy has it out for Akainu, obviously.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.180
Sanji’s kicks will have to stack up against
Kizaru’s lightspeed kicks.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.950
Zoro and Fujitora both have swords - a match
made in heaven.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:08.950
Hmmm…and what about Greenbull?

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:13.430
Well, we just learned that Aramaki is a highly
prejudiced individual and we happen to have

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:17.670
the powerful Fishman/Civil Rights advocate,
Jinbe, on the crew.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:23.319
It’s not much a monster trio anymore, but
we’re looking forward to the Admirals vs.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:24.790
the Monster Quartet.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.879
**One Piece was the Friends we Made Along
the Way**

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:30.140
What is the One Piece?

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:35.150
Well, the greatest fear among the fans is
that the One Piece…is nothing.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.830
There is not treasure - no world shaking revelations.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:42.379
Like the old saying goes - Life is a journey,
not a destination.

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:45.690
Finding the One Piece was never about material
gain.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.780
That’s why all of the treasure seekers who
only sought riches were doomed to fail, but

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:56.150
the adventurous Luffy and his crew who only
wanted freedom will be the ones to attain

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.150
it.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.970
The *real* treasure was the adventures they
had and all of the friends they made.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:08.959
Hmm… now that I think about it, the treasure
being nothing actually fits really well thematically.

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:13.360
But thankfully Oda Sensei has gone on record
saying that the One Piece *is* a physical,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.360
tangible treasure.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.840
So thank goodness, the cop-out ending has
been avoided and we’re getting something

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.440
cool and shiny in a few years!

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.430
**Dragon Wind Logia**

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.349
Normal absentee fathers go out to buy milk.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:30.940
*Real* absentee fathers go out to wage war
against an oppressive government.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.379
When Luffy finally met *his* absentee father
in Loguetown, he was accompanied by a powerful

00:03:36.379 --> 00:03:40.049
gale that enabled the Straw Hats’ escape
from Captain Smoker.

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:47.739
This very convenient wind (tinged green in
the anime) seemed almost supernaturally fortunate.

00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:53.770
Well, our best guess is that while the winds
were supernatural - they weren’t supernaturally

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:59.299
lucky - they were just supernatural in the
sense that they were the result of Dragon’s

00:03:59.299 --> 00:04:03.070
devil fruit power, which is likely a Wind
or Storm fruit.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:07.370
After all, this revolutionary who wants to
overturn the status quo could be said to bring

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:12.890
the “winds of change” - we all know Oda’s
up for some good wordplay after all.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.879
**Zoro is from Wano**

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:18.180
This popular theory is *pretty* much confirmed.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.049
Zoro was from an island named after the Shimotsuki
clan.

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:26.229
He definitely has some lineage here, but what
we would still love some answers on is who

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:28.889
exactly he’s descended from.

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:32.340
He looks exactly like the former Daimyo of
the Shimotsuki, Ushimaru.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:37.669
However, Oda has gone out of his way in an
SBS to deny that Zoro is Ushimaru’s son

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:41.520
despite very directly and obviously hinting
at it in the manga.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.009
So is he a nephew?

00:04:44.009 --> 00:04:45.260
A grandson?

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.850
Just tell us who he is, Oda, we’re begging
you!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.139
**Carrot for Nakama**

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:54.870
People seem to think that the hope for this
rabbit mink joining the crew is dead in the

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:55.870
water.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:59.150
She didn’t stow away when the crew left
Wano, shirking her responsibility as the new

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.530
ruler of Zou.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.539
Instead, Caribou was in the barrel.

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:07.449
Oda even played with our hearts and mocked
us by having the Sunny use a special new technique

00:05:07.449 --> 00:05:13.660
- the rabbit screw, in which the ship is propelled
by a barrel-housed propeller that looks like

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.660
a rabbit.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.300
But did you even consider this?

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.610
Yeah, sure Caribou is in the barrel, but you
know what?

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:23.630
Caribou can also fit a lot of barrels inside
him.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.110
And what’s in those barrels?

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.110
Carrot, probably.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:31.250
I will not give up hope that Carrot is still
stowed away inside of Caribou’s swamp until

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.710
we get a direct refutation of this theory.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.949
Never give up on Carrot because she’ll never
give up on you.

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:39.860
**Sanji is a Prince**

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.850
Give yourselves a round of applause One Piece
fans.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.350
You got this one right!

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:49.889
Before the Whole Cake Island arc, tons of
fans predicted that Sanji would turn out to

00:05:49.889 --> 00:05:51.460
be a prince.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:56.850
All the way back in the Baroque Works saga,
he assumed the secret identity: Mr. Prince.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:06:01.710
The theory went that this was more than a
nickname - this “secret identity” held

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.690
a big secret after all.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.539
In actuality, Sanji was a prince.

00:06:07.539 --> 00:06:13.210
Later, we received news that Sanji was actually
from North Blue and had somehow ended up in

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.460
the East Blue with Zeff.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.310
During the confrontation with Kuma, Sanji
revealed that he’d be the one to cause the

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.610
Straw Hats the most trouble down the line.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.550
There was the running gag that every single
one of Sanji’s wanted posters didn’t actually

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.470
show his face for one reason or another.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:33.440
However, in Dressrosa as soon as Sanji’s
real face was shown, his bounty condition

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:39.259
was changed to “Only Alive”, proving that
he was connected to someone with a lot of

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:41.800
power in the One Piece world.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:46.880
Finally, we learned that Sanji was in fact
a prince of the Germa Kingdom, proving many

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.759
eagle-eyed fans 100% correct.

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:53.099
**Garp is the leader of SWORD**

00:06:53.099 --> 00:06:57.490
SWORD is a secret organization within the
Marines with the aim of making the Marines

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:03.490
a force for good in the world instead of a
force for propping up the Celestial Dragons.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:08.500
Since two of the prominently known members
of SWORD are Koby and Helmeppo, who notably

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:14.620
trained directly under Monkey D. Garp, logic
would follow that Garp is the secret leader

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.819
of the organization.

00:07:15.819 --> 00:07:17.560
**7 Moons**

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:22.479
We know that Minks turn Sulong under the full
moon and that Enel is chilling out on a moon

00:07:22.479 --> 00:07:26.650
- but a more important question is…which
one?

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:31.840
In the Library of Ohara, we can see a model
of the One Piece planet and its orbiting satellites

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.240
that clearly show seven moons.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:39.150
If this is the case, does the world still
have all of these moons or were some destroyed

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.150
somehow.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:43.900
Or do we just conveniently never see more
than one in the sky at once?

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:49.180
Hopefully the scientific mastermind Vegapunk
drops some moon knowledge on us very soon.**Enel’s

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.180
Return**

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:53.960
And speaking of moons - Enel is up to something
on the moon.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:58.889
In his cover story he reached “Fairy Vearth”
and found the ruins of an ancient civilization

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:02.259
that seem to hold illustrations of the Ancient
Weapons.

00:08:02.259 --> 00:08:06.419
He also used his devil fruit to power up a
bunch of long dormant automatons.

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:10.449
All this, and he also even met bonafide space
pirates.

00:08:10.449 --> 00:08:16.509
So clearly, Enel is going to play into the
story again somehow, as so many cover story

00:08:16.509 --> 00:08:17.800
characters do.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:22.680
So how exactly are the Straw Hats going to
encounter this God again?

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:25.419
Is he going to strike down back to earth with
a robot army?

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:29.979
Or are the Strawhats - much like Gamestop
Stock - going to the MOON!?

00:08:29.979 --> 00:08:35.900
**Tenth Titanic Captain Aokiji**The Blackbeard
Pirates have Ten Titanic Captains, but we

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:38.750
have yet to find out who the tenth is.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:43.830
So far we only know of 9 Blackbeard crew members
(plus Blackbeard himself, but since Burgess

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.410
is the 1st captain, Teach doesn’t factor
into the count).

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:52.450
There have been a lot of wild guesses for
who this final Blackbeard crew member could

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:58.020
be, but the prevailing theory is the former
Marine Admiral Aokiji.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:02.600
Seeing Kuzan go fully onto the Blackbeard
crew and abandon his sense of justice is a

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:07.930
wild idea, but we do know that Aokiji is currently
allied with them in some capacity.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:14.350
Having him on their side would also hugely
increase the stakes when it’s finally time

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:17.750
for the Straw Hats to fight their crew.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.490
**Monster Point-Awakened Zoan**

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.140
It’s heavily implied that the Impel Down
jailers are Awakened Zoans.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:28.070
If that’s so, they’d be the first awakened
devil fruit users that we ever saw in the

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:30.010
series.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:34.700
UNLESS there’s actually one we saw first
- and wouldn’t you know it, they were actually

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.779
a member of the Straw Hat crew.

00:09:36.779 --> 00:09:42.890
Chopper ingesting three rumble balls might
have triggered a forced Zoan awakening.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:47.980
Monster Point may in fact have been the first
devil fruit awakening we ever saw in the series.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:48.980
**TIER 2**

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.019
All of this - and we haven’t even scratched
the surface.

00:09:52.019 --> 00:09:56.420
You probably know all of these theories and
easter eggs already.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:01.730
But now get ready to hold your breath because
we’re diving down to see what the One Piece

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.130
Iceberg holds in Tier 2.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:05.750
**Shanks Davy Back Fight**

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:10.950
Among One Piece’s “so-called fans” there
are lots of people who think the Davy Back

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:15.600
Fight and the Long-Ring-Long-Land arc are
boring and unimportant.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:18.779
Real fans, of course, believe in Foxy supremacy.

00:10:18.779 --> 00:10:24.330
We also know that Oda-Sensei doesn’t have
any unimportant arcs - just look at all of

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.420
the Skypiea deniers now.

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.880
So how will the Davy Back Fight play into
the story again?

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:34.230
Well, when it comes time for Shanks and Luffy
to finally meet again, this theory has it

00:10:45.785 --> 00:10:49.545
the Roger and Luffy - the former and the future
pirate king.

00:10:49.545 --> 00:10:51.865
The straw hat belonged to Roger.

00:10:51.865 --> 00:10:53.565
They share the same secret dream.

00:10:53.565 --> 00:10:56.175
So why not the same devil fruit?

00:10:56.175 --> 00:11:01.345
This long-held theory believed that the former
owner of the Gomu-Gomu no Mi was none other

00:11:01.345 --> 00:11:02.925
than Gol D. Roger.

00:11:02.925 --> 00:11:07.385
However, Kaidou’s recent statement that
Roger didn’t have any devil fruit powers

00:11:07.385 --> 00:11:10.355
seems to disprove this theory.

00:11:10.355 --> 00:11:13.825
We can say goodbye for our hopes for a stretchy
Roger.

00:11:13.825 --> 00:11:16.165
**Usopp’s Lies Come True**

00:11:16.165 --> 00:11:18.215
The pirates attacking Syrup Village.

00:11:18.215 --> 00:11:19.404
The Giant Goldfish.

00:11:19.404 --> 00:11:20.404
A huge mole.

00:11:20.404 --> 00:11:23.024
[Miss Merry Christmas] A beautiful swordsman
with meat.

00:11:23.024 --> 00:11:24.024
[Rebecca].

00:11:24.024 --> 00:11:28.774
Usopp has told many lies throughout the series
and one theory holds that by the end of the

00:11:28.774 --> 00:11:32.445
story all of these lies will come true.

00:11:32.445 --> 00:11:35.115
If that’s the case…are they really lies?

00:11:35.115 --> 00:11:37.264
One major lie we still need to see come true?

00:11:37.264 --> 00:11:40.225
Usopp leading an army 8000 strong.

00:11:40.225 --> 00:11:45.535
We got close in Dressrosa, but we still need
to pump up those numbers so let’s cross

00:11:45.535 --> 00:11:47.375
our fingers for Elbaf.

00:11:47.375 --> 00:11:48.375
**Kuina=Tashigi**

00:11:48.375 --> 00:11:54.035
Zoro’s childhood friend, Kuina, was the
catalyst for his dream.

00:11:54.035 --> 00:11:58.255
Every day that he strives to accomplish his
dream of becoming the world’s greatest swordsman,

00:11:58.255 --> 00:12:02.125
he does it because of the promise he made
to her.

00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:05.665
However, what if she wasn’t dead after all?

00:12:05.665 --> 00:12:10.774
What if, after losing her memories, she actually
grew up to become his marine rival Tashigi,

00:12:10.774 --> 00:12:12.345
the secondhand to Smoker?

00:12:12.345 --> 00:12:17.295
It wouldn’t be Oda’s first time using
amnesia as a plot point: looking at you Big

00:12:17.295 --> 00:12:19.005
Mom and Sabo.

00:12:19.005 --> 00:12:23.795
After all, Tashigi looks just like Kuina and
has a similar love of swords.

00:12:23.795 --> 00:12:29.154
Is it a coincidence or is there more to the
story?

00:12:29.154 --> 00:12:31.745
**Luffy will get Roger’s Disease**

00:12:31.745 --> 00:12:35.225
Before Roger’s execution, he was diagnosed
with an incurable disease.

00:12:35.225 --> 00:12:39.776
In the ongoing list of things that Luffy has
inherited from Roger, will he, too, contract

00:12:39.776 --> 00:12:40.875
“PirateKing-Itis”?

00:12:40.875 --> 00:12:46.245
Will the story end just like it began - with
the death of a pirate king?

00:12:46.245 --> 00:12:50.454
We have, after all, gotten lots and lots of
hints throughout the story about Luffy shortening

00:12:50.454 --> 00:12:51.635
his life span.

00:12:51.635 --> 00:12:53.635
Gear 2nd shortens his life span.

00:12:53.635 --> 00:12:56.805
His adrenaline treatments from Ivankov shortened
his life span.

00:12:56.805 --> 00:13:02.295
A side effect of Gear 5 appeared to be temporarily
transforming into an old man.

00:13:02.295 --> 00:13:05.045
Will this spell the end for Luffy?

00:13:05.045 --> 00:13:09.954
Is this exertion related to the incurable
disease that Roger had?

00:13:09.954 --> 00:13:18.005
Good thing the Thousand Sunny’s doctor has
a goal of curing every disease in the world.

00:13:18.005 --> 00:13:19.144
**Roger’s Egg**

00:13:19.144 --> 00:13:23.765
In many flashbacks we can see a massive egg
incubating on the back of Roger’s ship,

00:13:23.765 --> 00:13:25.464
the Oro Jackson.

00:13:25.464 --> 00:13:27.765
What could have hatched from a huge egg?

00:13:27.765 --> 00:13:28.765
Was it Marco?

00:13:28.765 --> 00:13:29.765
A dragon?

00:13:29.765 --> 00:13:31.475
Was it related to the ancient weapon Uranus?

00:13:31.475 --> 00:13:34.745
Could the One Piece be the world’s largest
omelet?

00:13:34.745 --> 00:13:38.834
Many theories have *hatched* from this giant
egg.

00:13:38.834 --> 00:13:39.995
The most likely theory?

00:13:39.995 --> 00:13:43.305
It was simply Tamago taking a nap.

00:13:43.305 --> 00:13:45.535
**Luffy 5,600,000,000**

00:13:45.535 --> 00:13:51.225
In Japanese, Gomu means rubber or gum - as
in the Gomu Gomu no Mi.

00:13:51.225 --> 00:13:55.824
However, the words Go-Mu can also be read
as the number 56.

00:13:55.824 --> 00:14:00.325
Therefore, Oda has long associated the number
56 with Luffy.

00:14:00.325 --> 00:14:03.885
As a child, he’s seen wearing a shirt with
the number 56 on it.

00:14:03.885 --> 00:14:06.135
Lucy’s coliseum number was 0556.

00:14:06.135 --> 00:14:09.524
There are 56 members of the Barto Fan Club.

00:14:09.524 --> 00:14:12.134
The Grand Fleet numbers over 5,600.

00:14:12.134 --> 00:14:18.555
Since Roger’s final bounty was revealed
to be a little over 5.5 billion, this theory

00:14:18.555 --> 00:14:24.005
predicts that Luffy’s final bounty will
surpass Roger’s and also keep with the theme

00:14:24.005 --> 00:14:26.154
of Luffy being associated with the number
56.

00:14:26.154 --> 00:14:30.964
He’ll likely have a final bounty of 5.6
billion berries.

00:14:30.964 --> 00:14:32.435
**Immortality Surgery**

00:14:32.435 --> 00:14:36.925
In Dressrosa, we learned that Law’s Ope-Ope
no Mi has a special ability.

00:14:36.925 --> 00:14:43.145
In exchange for the user’s life, they can
perform the immortality surgery, making their

00:14:43.145 --> 00:14:45.125
target immortal.

00:14:45.125 --> 00:14:50.835
We don’t have much additional information
about the exact mechanics of this insane ability,

00:14:50.835 --> 00:14:55.435
but this doesn’t seem like the thing that
Oda - king of foreshadowing - would casually

00:14:55.435 --> 00:14:58.214
drop and then never bring up again.

00:14:58.214 --> 00:15:02.105
Forget Chekhov’s Gun - this is Chekhov’s
Nuke.

00:15:02.105 --> 00:15:07.185
As for who Law may end up sacrificing his
life for, it’s a mystery.

00:15:07.185 --> 00:15:11.214
Doflamingo wanted Law to use it on him, but
with the former Shichibukai locked up, it’s

00:15:11.214 --> 00:15:13.605
a good bet it’ll be someone else.

00:15:13.605 --> 00:15:17.205
Though, we don’t think Doflamingo will be
in Impel Down forever.

00:15:17.205 --> 00:15:24.975
Did a past user use this surgery on seemingly
ancient characters like Imu or the Gorosei?

00:15:24.975 --> 00:15:30.975
Will Law use it on Luffy to circumvent the
side effects of the aforementioned PirateKing-Itis?

00:15:30.975 --> 00:15:33.714
Or will someone more nefarious use it?

00:15:33.714 --> 00:15:37.454
Blackbeard’s confrontation with Law has
us worried…

00:15:37.454 --> 00:15:39.845
**Usopp Conqueror’s Haki**

00:15:39.845 --> 00:15:42.904
Usopp is the ultimate underdog in One Piece.

00:15:42.904 --> 00:15:47.375
In a world of super-powered beings, he’s
someone that us normal weakling humans can

00:15:47.375 --> 00:15:48.725
really relate to.

00:15:48.725 --> 00:15:52.645
However, in addition to his insane stamina
and pain tolerance [show his skull being shattered

00:15:52.645 --> 00:15:56.285
by Mr. 4], he’s also been shown to have
some incredible feats.

00:15:56.285 --> 00:16:01.285
Namely, he unlocked observation haki when
he stopped Sugar from transforming Luffy and

00:16:01.285 --> 00:16:02.855
Law into toys on Dressrosa.

00:16:02.855 --> 00:16:08.214
Usopp’s ultimate goal is to become a brave
warrior of the sea and he’s teased leading

00:16:08.214 --> 00:16:10.764
armies 8,000 soldiers strong.

00:16:10.764 --> 00:16:15.395
While he does seem to be a fearful coward,
he’s courageous in that he always overcomes

00:16:15.395 --> 00:16:19.964
his fear to take on opponents many times stronger
than himself.

00:16:19.964 --> 00:16:26.125
That sounds like a conqueror to me - so maybe
Usopp will join Luffy and Zoro as a member

00:16:26.125 --> 00:16:30.285
of the Straw Hats that can use the rarest
form of Haki.

00:16:30.285 --> 00:16:35.324
**The Straw** **Hat is the One Piece**

00:16:35.324 --> 00:16:36.405
What is the One Piece?

00:16:36.405 --> 00:16:38.184
It’s not the friends we made along the way.

00:16:38.184 --> 00:16:39.954
That would just be silly.

00:16:39.954 --> 00:16:45.184
Obviously, it’s the great treasure that
Luffy has had all along.

00:16:45.184 --> 00:16:49.725
As far back as Orange Town, after Buggy stabbed
through the straw hat, we learned that it

00:16:49.725 --> 00:16:53.045
was Luffy’s most prized possession - his
treasure.

00:16:53.045 --> 00:16:59.695
How then, could even finding Roger’s treasure
- the One Piece - surpass the treasure Luffy’s

00:16:59.695 --> 00:17:00.885
always had.

00:17:00.885 --> 00:17:03.845
But this theory works more than just on a
metaphorical level.

00:17:03.845 --> 00:17:06.855
What if the straw hat is genuinely important.

00:17:06.855 --> 00:17:10.015
We know that the hat passed from Roger to
Shanks to Luffy.

00:17:10.015 --> 00:17:16.045
We also know that Imu-Sama has a massive straw
hat in cold storage.

00:17:16.045 --> 00:17:20.125
Somehow the hat is obviously connected to
the ancient history and the void century,

00:17:20.125 --> 00:17:25.005
so is it going too far to think that the hat
is the One Piece itself?

00:17:25.005 --> 00:17:27.505
**Scopper visited Crocus**

00:17:27.505 --> 00:17:32.755
Once upon a time in a fateful cover story
that would spawn theory after theory, we were

00:17:32.755 --> 00:17:38.565
treated to everyone’s favorite whale doctor,
Crocus, chatting it up with a mysterious figure.

00:17:38.565 --> 00:17:43.505
The figure was dressed in an Amigasa straw
hat and Wano-style robes, giving the impression

00:17:43.505 --> 00:17:46.615
that this character would be connected to
Wano.

00:17:46.615 --> 00:17:52.115
However, the Wano arc came and went with no
reveal to speak of.

00:17:52.115 --> 00:17:56.135
Since Crocus was the doctor for the Roger
pirates, one leading idea for the identity

00:17:56.135 --> 00:17:59.775
for this character is none other than Scopper
Gaban.

00:17:59.775 --> 00:18:04.585
After other former Roger pirates like Rayleigh
have become important players in the story,

00:18:04.585 --> 00:18:10.554
it seems like it would only make sense to
introduce Scopper into the story.

00:18:10.554 --> 00:18:15.176
He’s featured prominently in many of the
Roger flashbacks, but we still haven’t met

00:18:15.176 --> 00:18:17.294
him in the current timeline.

00:18:17.294 --> 00:18:21.355
At this rate, will we ever meet Roger’s
3rd in command?

00:18:21.355 --> 00:18:26.535
**Admiral Koby**It’s unlikely that Akainu
will promote Koby to become one of the highest

00:18:26.535 --> 00:18:27.875
military powers.

00:18:27.875 --> 00:18:33.355
And besides - pink isn’t on the color wheel,
so how would Koby possibly fit in with the

00:18:33.355 --> 00:18:36.365
current naming conventions of the admirals.

00:18:36.365 --> 00:18:41.915
He doesn’t even have an uber-powerful logia
devil fruit, either.However, Koby’s dream

00:18:41.915 --> 00:18:44.255
is to become a Marine Admiral.

00:18:44.255 --> 00:18:47.095
By the end of the series, he will.

00:18:47.095 --> 00:18:50.525
One Piece is a series where characters we
love achieve their dreams.

00:18:50.525 --> 00:18:55.005
If the end of the series sees a reformation
of the Marines to become a true force for

00:18:55.005 --> 00:18:59.924
justice in the world, SWORD will likely lead
that transformation.

00:18:59.924 --> 00:19:04.365
And with them, Koby may become one of the
leaders of the Marines.

00:19:04.365 --> 00:19:05.365
**Zunisha is Pluton**

00:19:05.365 --> 00:19:11.335
In Fishman Island, we learned that the ancient
weapon Poseidon was not a physical object,

00:19:11.335 --> 00:19:13.325
but a living person.

00:19:13.325 --> 00:19:18.405
Unlike Pluton, which we’d heard was a warship,
Poseidon was actually the mermaid princess

00:19:18.405 --> 00:19:22.265
Shirahoshi and her power to control the Sea
Kings.

00:19:22.265 --> 00:19:27.225
In Wano, we learned that Pluton is actually
housed beneath Wano.

00:19:27.225 --> 00:19:30.655
However, we haven’t laid eyes on it yet.

00:19:30.655 --> 00:19:35.284
Perhaps the real story is more complicated
and Momonosuke’s ability to communicate

00:19:35.284 --> 00:19:41.655
with and command the giant elephant Zunisha
is somehow connected with the ancient weapon

00:19:41.655 --> 00:19:42.655
Pluton.

00:19:42.655 --> 00:19:44.674
**Devil Fruits are Man Made**

00:19:44.674 --> 00:19:51.005
Dr. Vegapunk and Caesar Clown’s SMILE technology
has allowed the criminal underworld to produce

00:19:51.005 --> 00:19:52.424
artificial devil fruits.

00:19:52.424 --> 00:19:56.595
Most of them are pale reflections of a true
devil fruit’s capabilities, and many of

00:19:56.595 --> 00:19:58.755
them are outright defective.

00:19:58.755 --> 00:20:03.075
However, what if *all* devil fruits are actually
artificial.

00:20:03.075 --> 00:20:09.025
What if these magic fruits are actually scientific
creations of the Ancient Kingdom?

00:20:09.025 --> 00:20:13.595
Perhaps devil fruits didn’t just occur as
a byproduct of nature, but were specifically

00:20:13.595 --> 00:20:19.144
cultivated and created to imbue great powers
upon those who eat the fruits.

00:20:19.144 --> 00:20:23.914
When Vegapunk cracked the code to recreating
Kaidou’s fruit, he wasn’t imitating nature,

00:20:23.914 --> 00:20:27.934
but recreating an ancient technology.

00:20:27.934 --> 00:20:31.445
**Weevil is Whitebeard’s Real Son**

00:20:31.445 --> 00:20:36.135
When we were first introduced to Edward Weevil,
the only Shichibukai who didn’t get to accomplish

00:20:36.135 --> 00:20:42.915
a single thing in the story before the Warlord
system was disbanded, we had a lot of thoughts.

00:20:42.915 --> 00:20:48.605
Thoughts such as “what is this guy’s deal”
and “there’s no way this clown is Whitebeard’s

00:20:48.605 --> 00:20:49.605
son.”

00:20:49.605 --> 00:20:53.845
Oda, however, likes to write his story in
a way that keeps us constantly surprised.

00:20:53.845 --> 00:20:57.485
What would the most surprising reveal be in
relation to Weevil?

00:20:57.485 --> 00:21:01.115
Well, that this wasn’t a lie after all.

00:21:01.115 --> 00:21:03.415
Mr. Newgate - you are the father.

00:21:03.415 --> 00:21:04.415
[including a snippet of Maury might be fun
here]

00:21:04.415 --> 00:21:05.415
**TIER 3**

00:21:05.415 --> 00:21:06.415
Oh, are these theories not enough for you?

00:21:06.415 --> 00:21:08.375
Well we’re only just now getting started.

00:21:08.375 --> 00:21:13.575
We’ve stuck our heads under the water and
now it’s time to start swimming because

00:21:13.575 --> 00:21:16.174
we’ve arrived at Tier 3.

00:21:16.174 --> 00:21:18.565
**The Raid will Fail**

00:21:18.565 --> 00:21:24.705
Viewers of a certain Mr. Morj will be familiar
with this theory.

00:21:24.705 --> 00:21:28.985
Once upon a time, fans hoped for a 5 act structure
to the Wano arc.

00:21:28.985 --> 00:21:34.015
However as Act 3 stretched on longer…and
longer…and longer…it became evident that

00:21:34.015 --> 00:21:36.655
we were in the climax of the arc.

00:21:36.655 --> 00:21:41.605
The theory went based on the 5 act structure
of many Kabuki plays, which says that at the

00:21:41.605 --> 00:21:47.914
end of the 3rd act there’s a great tragedy,
followed by a final battle in act 4 and a

00:21:47.914 --> 00:21:49.764
resolution in act 5.

00:21:49.764 --> 00:21:54.015
We kept waiting for our great tragedy - We
thought perhaps the Scabbards’ defeat by

00:21:54.015 --> 00:21:55.605
Kaidou would be the tragedy.

00:21:55.605 --> 00:22:00.125
We thought that maybe Luffy being thrown into
the sea was the tragedy.

00:22:00.125 --> 00:22:04.255
We thought that Luffy’s literal death was
the tragedy.

00:22:04.255 --> 00:22:09.705
The idea, popularized and the meme-ified by
Mr. Morj’s channel, was that after a loss

00:22:09.705 --> 00:22:14.735
during the raid, the allies would have to
recoup their losses and then train to fight

00:22:14.735 --> 00:22:18.175
another day before ultimately beating Kaidou.

00:22:18.175 --> 00:22:22.924
However, in the end, Oda once again defied
our expectations.

00:22:22.924 --> 00:22:25.764
**Mythical Cerberus Zoan**

00:22:25.764 --> 00:22:27.805
Blackbeard always works in threes.

00:22:27.805 --> 00:22:29.465
He has three skulls on his flag.

00:22:29.465 --> 00:22:30.645
He has three pistols.

00:22:30.645 --> 00:22:34.105
He left three scars on Shanks’ face.

00:22:34.105 --> 00:22:38.465
This popular theory says that in addition
to his Darkness Logia and Earthquake Paramecia

00:22:38.465 --> 00:22:44.005
fruit, Blackbeard has a third fruit: one that
allows him to have three different devil fruits

00:22:44.005 --> 00:22:45.575
in the first place.

00:22:45.575 --> 00:22:49.145
He has a mythical dog zoan: Model Cerberus.

00:22:49.145 --> 00:22:53.654
This three headed dog of legend just works
too well for the “three” motif that Blackbeard

00:22:53.654 --> 00:22:55.914
has going for him.

00:22:55.914 --> 00:22:59.665
**Law is in SWORD**

00:22:59.665 --> 00:23:03.335
This is another theory that’s part of a
specific YouTuber’s agenda.

00:23:03.335 --> 00:23:06.535
This idea was popularized by Randy Troy.

00:23:06.535 --> 00:23:10.605
Law may be playing the long con, being a secret
marine all along.

00:23:10.605 --> 00:23:15.475
It would mean that he takes after his mentor,
Rosinante, like so many other One Piece characters

00:23:15.475 --> 00:23:18.365
who also take after their mentors.

00:23:18.365 --> 00:23:22.895
This secret identity would also make sense
given the interactions between X-Drake, another

00:23:22.895 --> 00:23:25.465
SWORD member, and Law on Wano.

00:23:25.465 --> 00:23:30.095
Their cryptic conversation seemed to reveal
a sort of connection.

00:23:30.095 --> 00:23:34.245
Another piece of evidence for the theory deals
with the mysterious Rocky Port incident, which

00:23:34.245 --> 00:23:40.265
gave Law the reputation to become a Shichibukai,
and in which Koby, another SWORD member, played

00:23:40.265 --> 00:23:41.345
the hero.

00:23:41.345 --> 00:23:44.085
**Straw Hat Devil Fruit**

00:23:44.085 --> 00:23:49.805
For those of you who were not weekly during
Dressrosa, this may surprise you.

00:23:49.805 --> 00:23:54.825
When the Mera-Mera no Mi was up for grabs
there was no shortage of theories for who

00:23:54.825 --> 00:23:57.344
would receive the fruit.

00:23:57.344 --> 00:24:02.804
Some theories were Sanji, who had already
been seen to use flames, or even Franky…for

00:24:02.804 --> 00:24:03.804
some reason.

00:24:03.804 --> 00:24:08.424
Sabo hadn’t yet re-entered the story and
there was no telling when or if this other

00:24:08.424 --> 00:24:09.664
brother would return.

00:24:09.664 --> 00:24:14.475
There were even many theories that an antagonist
would eat the fruit, leading to Luffy having

00:24:14.475 --> 00:24:19.654
to fight against his brother’s fruit.However,
one of the wildest speculations to come out

00:24:19.654 --> 00:24:24.135
of this time was that Luffy’s Straw Hat
would get a devil fruit.

00:24:24.135 --> 00:24:27.615
Luffy himself, of course, couldn’t eat the
fruit since he’d already eaten the Gomu

00:24:27.615 --> 00:24:28.615
Gomu no Mi.

00:24:28.615 --> 00:24:33.685
However, ever since Alabasta we’ve known
that inanimate objects are able to consume

00:24:33.685 --> 00:24:34.685
devil fruits.

00:24:34.685 --> 00:24:41.015
This led a ton of people to believe that the
Straw Hat would gain the power to become fire,

00:24:41.015 --> 00:24:45.054
allowing Luffy and Ace to continue fighting
alongside each other in a way.

00:24:45.054 --> 00:24:50.125
But hey, who knows, maybe it’s not too late
for the Straw Hat to get another fruit.

00:24:50.125 --> 00:24:52.065
**Vegapunk Revolutionary**

00:24:52.065 --> 00:24:57.284
Why would Kuma, a revolutionary, willingly
let Vegapunk turn him into a mindless machine

00:24:57.284 --> 00:25:00.725
that does the bidding of the world government.

00:25:00.725 --> 00:25:05.184
According to this theory, it’s because Vegapunk
has always been playing both sides of the

00:25:05.184 --> 00:25:06.184
conflict.

00:25:06.184 --> 00:25:09.945
While they’re happy to accept the government’s
research and development funding, they may

00:25:09.945 --> 00:25:12.684
not agree politically with the government’s
aims.

00:25:12.684 --> 00:25:17.794
They might, in fact, want to use their technology
to make the world a better place and only

00:25:17.794 --> 00:25:22.955
make weapons in a trade-off that allows them
to fund the research they really want to do.

00:25:22.955 --> 00:25:33.125
It’s possible that Kuma still retains some
of his old will.

00:25:33.125 --> 00:25:37.745
After all, before going full Pacifista he
was able to send the Straw Hats to their timeskip

00:25:37.745 --> 00:25:40.495
destinations as well as guarding the Thousand
Sunny.

00:25:40.495 --> 00:25:44.414
Surely we’ll learn more about Vegapunk’s
allegiances during the Egghead Island arc.

00:25:44.414 --> 00:25:47.414
**The D is for Dawn**

00:25:47.414 --> 00:25:48.965
Monkey D. Luffy.

00:25:48.965 --> 00:25:50.105
Portgas D. Ace.

00:25:50.105 --> 00:25:51.465
Jaguar D. Saul.

00:25:51.465 --> 00:25:54.924
Those with the D initial are the natural enemy
of God.

00:25:54.924 --> 00:25:57.705
The Celestial Dragons fear these members of
the D clan.

00:25:57.705 --> 00:26:01.105
But, what exactly does the D stand for?

00:26:01.105 --> 00:26:02.105
Destiny?

00:26:02.105 --> 00:26:03.105
Destruction?

00:26:03.105 --> 00:26:04.105
Death?

00:26:04.105 --> 00:26:05.105
Despair?

00:26:05.105 --> 00:26:06.105
Delirium?

00:26:06.105 --> 00:26:07.105
Desire?

00:26:07.105 --> 00:26:08.105
Dream?

00:26:08.105 --> 00:26:09.105
[Gaiman’s Sandman reference] Well, no, it’s
probably not one of the seven endless - it’s

00:26:09.105 --> 00:26:10.294
the wrong series for that.

00:26:10.294 --> 00:26:15.725
Instead, we should look to the original One
Piece one shot…and the title of the first

00:26:15.725 --> 00:26:18.285
chapter of the series: Romance Dawn.

00:26:18.285 --> 00:26:24.645
Luffy, the new JoyBoy, is foretold to bring
a new Dawn of the World, so what likelier

00:26:24.645 --> 00:26:26.904
candidate than this for Luffy’s middle name?

00:26:26.904 --> 00:26:27.904
**Con D. Oriano**

00:26:27.904 --> 00:26:35.785
A lesser known member of the D clan and one
of the strongest in the verse is, of course,

00:26:35.785 --> 00:26:37.054
Con D. Oriano.

00:26:37.054 --> 00:26:42.315
Much like how Trafalgar D. Waterlaw hid his
true name under the guise of Trafalgar Law,

00:26:42.315 --> 00:26:47.265
Con D. Oriano hid his D initial by going by
the name Condoriano.

00:26:47.265 --> 00:26:51.775
For those unaware, Con D. Oriano is a member
of the Straw Hat crew that made his first

00:26:51.775 --> 00:26:58.125
appearance in the G-8 arc - the only anime
filler arc that might as well be canon according

00:26:58.125 --> 00:26:59.394
to the fandom.

00:26:59.394 --> 00:27:04.985
This mighty member of the D clan single handedly
saved the Straw Hats and enabled them to escape

00:27:04.985 --> 00:27:10.995
the G-8 base by bravely allowing himself to
be imprisoned while Robin went on an espionage

00:27:10.995 --> 00:27:11.995
mission.

00:27:11.995 --> 00:27:15.424
Will Oda ever make Condoriano manga canon?

00:27:15.424 --> 00:27:16.934
We can only hope so.

00:27:16.934 --> 00:27:19.325
**Shanks Celestial Dragon**

00:27:19.325 --> 00:27:23.035
This red-haired Yonkou is hiding something
big.

00:27:23.035 --> 00:27:27.914
What kind of pirate is allowed to just waltz
into the Gorosei’s chambers to hold a private

00:27:27.914 --> 00:27:28.914
meeting?

00:27:28.914 --> 00:27:33.245
Well, the kind that is secretly a Celestial
Dragon.

00:27:33.245 --> 00:27:38.565
This longtime theory states that Shanks is
more than just a friendly, party-loving mentor

00:27:38.565 --> 00:27:39.565
to Luffy.

00:27:39.565 --> 00:27:43.975
Instead, he has a more mysterious and sinister
past as a member of the Tenryubito.

00:27:43.975 --> 00:27:48.105
The timeline would suggest that Shanks was
an infant and would have come aboard Roger’s

00:27:48.105 --> 00:27:54.325
ship right around the time of God Valley,
so it’s very likely that he was “adopted”

00:27:54.325 --> 00:28:01.005
by Roger and was a survivor of that island’s
disappearance.

00:28:01.005 --> 00:28:06.785
**Big Mom and Beast Pirates in the Grand Fleet**

00:28:06.785 --> 00:28:09.135
The grand fleet isn’t over yet.

00:28:09.135 --> 00:28:14.385
Having the members of Orlumbus’s crew and
the Tontatta is one thing, but to finally

00:28:14.385 --> 00:28:19.255
take on the World Government, the Straw Hats
might need some heavier hitters.

00:28:19.255 --> 00:28:23.054
Enter the crews of the former Yonkou, Big
Mom and Kaidou.

00:28:23.054 --> 00:28:27.195
On Whole Cake Island, Luffy made an ally through
his hard-fought battle with Katakuri.

00:28:27.195 --> 00:28:32.404
The two, despite being on opposing sides,
came to recognize and respect each other deeply

00:28:32.404 --> 00:28:34.045
as individuals.

00:28:34.045 --> 00:28:39.135
In addition to Big Mom’s son becoming an
ally, Kaidou’s son, too, befriended Luffy.

00:28:39.135 --> 00:28:43.735
Yamato wanted to sail away with the crew,
but remained to act as Wano’s protector

00:28:43.735 --> 00:28:45.855
from outside forces.

00:28:45.855 --> 00:28:50.015
With these two Yonkou’s children as allies,
it’s likely that with Big Mom and Kaidou

00:28:50.015 --> 00:28:55.554
out of the picture, the remnants of these
crews could end up fighting on the Straw Hats’

00:28:55.554 --> 00:28:57.294
side in the final war.

00:28:57.294 --> 00:28:59.335
**Second Time Skip**

00:28:59.335 --> 00:29:04.225
Especially before the revelation that was
Gear 5, it was a mystery how the Straw Hats

00:29:04.225 --> 00:29:08.235
could ever contend with the seemingly invincible
Yonkou.

00:29:08.235 --> 00:29:11.804
Well, how did they deal with insurmountable
foes the last time?

00:29:11.804 --> 00:29:13.375
Through a time skip, of course.

00:29:13.375 --> 00:29:17.155
So why not Shippuden the Straw Hats a second
time?

00:29:17.155 --> 00:29:19.505
The real reason they didn’t go this route?

00:29:19.505 --> 00:29:22.005
Oda couldn’t figure out how to make Franky’s
shoulders any bigger.

00:29:22.005 --> 00:29:24.164
(Among other crew member’s body parts getting
bigger…)

00:29:24.164 --> 00:29:25.164
**Immortal Gorosei**

00:29:25.164 --> 00:29:29.105
A lot of characters in One Piece have flashbacks
where we can see depictions of their younger

00:29:29.105 --> 00:29:30.105
selves.

00:29:30.105 --> 00:29:34.475
We’re treated to younger “in their prime”
versions of older characters like Garp, Sengoku,

00:29:34.475 --> 00:29:35.475
or Whitebeard.

00:29:35.475 --> 00:29:40.095
And when appropriate, we see those characters
de-aged to children - we’ve seen Buggy and

00:29:40.095 --> 00:29:42.105
Shanks as kids, among many others.

00:29:42.105 --> 00:29:47.285
However, during Robin’s flashback we got
to see the Gorosei of approximately twenty

00:29:47.285 --> 00:29:51.294
years ago and they look…exactly the same.

00:29:51.294 --> 00:29:55.644
With Oda paying such good attention to the
timeline and drawing the details of characters

00:29:55.644 --> 00:30:00.554
aging, this seems too big to just be an oversight.

00:30:00.554 --> 00:30:05.684
The designs of the Five Elder Stars were already
old, but they have not changed even a tiny

00:30:05.684 --> 00:30:08.215
bit over that time span.

00:30:08.215 --> 00:30:11.255
That raises the question: Do they age at all?

00:30:11.255 --> 00:30:13.625
Or are the Gorosei immortal and unaging?

00:30:13.625 --> 00:30:18.914
Perhaps they are the same rulers of the World
Government that were around during the Void

00:30:18.914 --> 00:30:19.914
Century.

00:30:19.914 --> 00:30:22.674
**Brook is Kuzan’s Grandpa**

00:30:22.674 --> 00:30:25.414
They both have afros and ice powers.

00:30:25.414 --> 00:30:26.414
Need we say more?

00:30:26.414 --> 00:30:27.414
**Tier 4**

00:30:27.414 --> 00:30:31.015
As we sink deeper and deeper, the iceberg
only grows.

00:30:31.015 --> 00:30:34.975
Who could have predicted that what already
seemed so massive above the surface would

00:30:34.975 --> 00:30:37.585
contain such unseen multitudes?

00:30:37.585 --> 00:30:41.565
Do the depths of this fandom ever end?

00:30:41.565 --> 00:30:43.784
Our craft has reached…Tier 4.

00:30:43.784 --> 00:30:44.784
**CrocoMom**

00:30:44.784 --> 00:30:48.914
After Enies Lobby, Luffy learned that he has
a dad.

00:30:48.914 --> 00:30:54.395
This dad was none other than Monkey D. Dragon,
the most wanted man in the world - another

00:30:54.395 --> 00:30:58.345
thorn in the government’s side: Like father
like son.

00:30:58.345 --> 00:31:04.095
However, according to popular scientific sources,
in order to be born, a Shonen protagonist

00:31:04.095 --> 00:31:07.565
needs both a father *and* a mother.

00:31:07.565 --> 00:31:11.345
However, we have no clue who’s Luffy’s
mom is.

00:31:11.345 --> 00:31:13.115
Or do we???

00:31:13.115 --> 00:31:18.385
Oda has gone on record saying that he has
drawn Luffy’s mom in the series, so who

00:31:18.385 --> 00:31:19.405
could it be?

00:31:19.405 --> 00:31:23.135
Is it a background revolutionary still hanging
out with Dragon?

00:31:23.135 --> 00:31:27.155
Or is it someone we know much better: A certain
Sir Crocodile.

00:31:27.155 --> 00:31:34.195
As we learned earlier in the iceberg, Crocodile
was very likely assigned female at birth before

00:31:34.195 --> 00:31:39.885
crossing paths with Ivankov, a revolutionary
who would have been in proximity to Dragon.

00:31:39.885 --> 00:31:43.865
Before his transition, could he have had a
child with Dragon?

00:31:43.865 --> 00:31:45.815
A certain Luffy, perhaps?

00:31:45.815 --> 00:31:48.205
**Usopp is the Narrator**

00:31:48.205 --> 00:31:50.764
The narrator of One Piece is a curious figure.

00:31:50.764 --> 00:31:56.205
Our greatest literary scholars have tried
to intuit the exact identity of the narrator.

00:31:56.205 --> 00:32:00.715
At times, this person speaks of future events,
as if they are recalling the story from a

00:32:00.715 --> 00:32:04.225
later date and thus can foreshadow what’s
to come.

00:32:04.225 --> 00:32:08.635
A prime example of this is during the formation
of the Straw Hat Grand Fleet, when the narrator

00:32:08.635 --> 00:32:13.174
speaks of a cataclysmic event that they’ll
one day participate in.

00:32:13.174 --> 00:32:17.225
Is this narrator just a disembodied, omniscient
and omnipresent voice?

00:32:17.225 --> 00:32:20.595
Or is the narrator an actual character in
the story.

00:32:20.595 --> 00:32:25.985
This theory goes that the story of One Piece
is actually being told retroactively by Usopp.

00:32:25.985 --> 00:32:31.175
Hopefully, this story is just a little more
truthful than the ones he usually tells.

00:32:31.175 --> 00:32:32.775
**Charlotte Bonney**

00:32:32.775 --> 00:32:34.664
Bonney is Kuma’s daughter.

00:32:34.664 --> 00:32:37.405
She is a princess of the Sorbet kingdom.

00:32:37.405 --> 00:32:40.095
We know this now, but we didn’t always.

00:32:40.095 --> 00:32:43.294
But what we did know is that Bonney has pink
hair.

00:32:43.294 --> 00:32:45.605
Who else has pink hair?

00:32:45.605 --> 00:32:48.294
Charlotte Lin Lin: Big Mom herself.

00:32:48.294 --> 00:32:51.135
After all, Lola has pink hair and ended up
being Big Mom’s daughter.

00:32:51.135 --> 00:32:54.904
Come to think of it…we don’t know who
Bonney’s mother is.

00:32:54.904 --> 00:32:59.195
Has Kuma been one of Big Mom’s many ex-husbands
all along?

00:32:59.195 --> 00:33:01.075
**The Thousand Sunny is Pluton**

00:33:01.075 --> 00:33:05.585
I know we said at the beginning of the video
that we weren’t talking about that Iceberg

00:33:05.585 --> 00:33:09.575
[Show Iceberg the character], but for this
one we’re going to have to.

00:33:09.575 --> 00:33:14.565
During Water 7, CP9 was searching for the
blueprints to the ancient weapon, Pluton,

00:33:14.565 --> 00:33:17.794
a powerful warship capable of mass destruction.

00:33:17.794 --> 00:33:23.965
They thought that Iceberg had them, but in
actuality, it was his adopted brother Franky

00:33:23.965 --> 00:33:25.455
who had them.

00:33:25.455 --> 00:33:30.145
In order to protect them from falling into
the wrong hands, Franky burned the blueprints

00:33:30.145 --> 00:33:32.435
so that the government couldn’t obtain them.

00:33:32.435 --> 00:33:37.764
Later in the arc, Franky constructed the Straw
Hats’ new ship, the Thousand Sunny.

00:33:37.764 --> 00:33:43.764
Given Franky’s immense cyborg inventor brain,
it’s not unreasonable that he could have

00:33:43.764 --> 00:33:46.335
memorized Pluton’s blueprints.

00:33:46.335 --> 00:33:51.494
Could some of Pluton’s super-powerful features
have actually made it into the design of his

00:33:51.494 --> 00:33:53.825
dream ship, the Thousand Sunny?

00:33:53.825 --> 00:33:56.345
**Dragon is not Garp’s Son**

00:33:56.345 --> 00:34:00.875
Both of these One Piece powerhouses hold the
Monkey family name, but one theory states

00:34:00.875 --> 00:34:03.075
that they’re not actually blood related.

00:34:03.075 --> 00:34:09.135
While Garp is Luffy’s grandpa and Dragon
is Luffy’s father, it’s not as clear cut

00:34:09.135 --> 00:34:11.835
that Dragon is actually Garp’s son.

00:34:11.835 --> 00:34:16.375
Instead, Dragon could have married into the
Monkey family and much in the way that Ace

00:34:16.375 --> 00:34:21.115
took his mother’s last name, Dragon could
have taken his wife’s last name to hide

00:34:21.115 --> 00:34:26.035
some part of his heritage.After all, doesn’t
Dragon’s silhouette look suspiciously like

00:34:26.035 --> 00:34:27.925
that of Rocks D. Xebec?

00:34:27.925 --> 00:34:30.405
**Pirate King Buggy**

00:34:30.405 --> 00:34:35.484
Buggy D. Clown has been failing his way upwards
throughout the entire series.

00:34:35.484 --> 00:34:40.435
He started as a lowly pirate in East Blue,
but after his arrest, Luffy’s prison break

00:34:40.435 --> 00:34:45.065
enabled him to become one of the first pirates
to escape from Impel Down.

00:34:45.065 --> 00:34:49.875
Thanks to taking the credit for the mass escape
as well as his status as a former Roger crew

00:34:49.875 --> 00:34:54.805
member, he was able to elevate himself to
the lofty position of Shichibukai.

00:34:54.805 --> 00:34:59.315
Things took a turn for the worse for Buggy
when his giant crew members left to join the

00:34:59.315 --> 00:35:04.325
Straw Hat Grand Fleet and then the Shichibukai
system was outright dissolved.

00:35:04.325 --> 00:35:09.405
However, thanks to the Cross Guild, he’s
now cemented his status as one of the Four

00:35:09.405 --> 00:35:10.825
Emperors of the Sea.

00:35:10.825 --> 00:35:15.815
If the trend continues, we could see Buggy
become a bonafide King of the Pirates - at

00:35:15.815 --> 00:35:17.535
least temporarily.

00:35:17.535 --> 00:35:21.915
After all, doesn’t it just feel right for
this character to be present at Laugh Tale?

00:35:21.915 --> 00:35:26.645
He’s been alongside Luffy and has such a
history with Shanks that him being with us

00:35:26.645 --> 00:35:29.744
in the end just seems to make sense.

00:35:29.744 --> 00:35:33.525
Provided he doesn’t get an inconveniently
timed illness again, of course.

00:35:33.525 --> 00:35:36.255
**Marco will become an Egg**

00:35:36.255 --> 00:35:38.795
Marco the Phoenix can turn into a…phoenix.

00:35:38.795 --> 00:35:42.325
Wow, his epitaph is really on the nose, huh.

00:35:42.325 --> 00:35:48.116
Anyway, despite his cool healing prowess and
powers of flight, we still haven’t seen

00:35:48.116 --> 00:35:54.635
this pineapple activate the most famous of
phoenix powers: he still hasn’t died and

00:35:54.635 --> 00:35:55.925
been reborn.

00:35:55.925 --> 00:36:00.665
In the final war, will Marco be tragically
killed, only to avoid death and resurrect

00:36:00.665 --> 00:36:06.355
himself in the form of a brand new, far younger
Marco?We’re not satisfied with Baron Tamago

00:36:06.355 --> 00:36:11.645
being the only character with an egg-based
transformation and we will not be satisfied

00:36:11.645 --> 00:36:18.865
until Marco, too, dies and becomes an egg
and subsequently a tiny Marco baby.

00:36:18.865 --> 00:36:20.105
**Will of P**

00:36:20.105 --> 00:36:22.175
Listen, I don’t make the rules.

00:36:22.175 --> 00:36:27.415
If you’re a One Piece character and your
name starts with the letter “P”, you don’t

00:36:27.415 --> 00:36:28.795
get to die.

00:36:28.795 --> 00:36:32.714
Granted, most One Piece characters don’t
get to die unless they’re in a flashback,

00:36:32.714 --> 00:36:36.895
but this goes double for our “P” characters.

00:36:36.895 --> 00:36:40.945
Pell sacrificing himself to save Alabasta
from a massive bomb?

00:36:40.945 --> 00:36:41.974
No problem.

00:36:41.974 --> 00:36:44.315
Pell eats bombs for breakfast.

00:36:44.315 --> 00:36:50.505
Old man Pagaya, Conis’s dad, taking the
full brunt of Enel’s lightning powers?

00:36:50.505 --> 00:36:52.935
Maybe Luffy’s not the only rubber man after
all.

00:36:52.935 --> 00:36:58.335
Pekoms was riddled with bullet holes and dropped
into shark infested waters.

00:36:58.335 --> 00:37:01.295
Don’t worry, he’s alright, though.

00:37:01.295 --> 00:37:07.135
And, the newest member of the club: Pound
- he inexplicably survives the attacks of

00:37:07.135 --> 00:37:09.165
the Big Mom pirates.

00:37:09.165 --> 00:37:13.385
The Will of P is the only force in One Piece
that can rival the might of the Will of D.

00:37:13.385 --> 00:37:19.125
And this is why we’ll likely see our good
friend Pedro again in the near future.

00:37:19.125 --> 00:37:21.515
**Blackbeard will kill Shanks**

00:37:21.515 --> 00:37:24.375
We all know that Oda loves to make us cry.

00:37:24.375 --> 00:37:28.965
Oda also loves giving Luffy one million reasons
to punch Blackbeard.

00:37:28.965 --> 00:37:31.105
Blackbeard was largely responsible for Ace’s
death.

00:37:31.105 --> 00:37:34.575
He’s the chief rival for Luffy’s ultimate
goal, the One Piece.

00:37:34.575 --> 00:37:38.635
Blackbeard has captured Luffy’s good friend
Koby (and may do the same for his chief ally,

00:37:38.635 --> 00:37:39.635
Law).

00:37:39.635 --> 00:37:45.335
Moreover, they have different taste in pies
- a conflict that cannot be overcome by any

00:37:45.335 --> 00:37:47.494
means other than violence.

00:37:47.494 --> 00:37:51.915
We also know that Shanks and Blackbeard have
a history, having met each other all the way

00:37:51.915 --> 00:37:53.535
back during childhood.

00:37:53.535 --> 00:37:57.335
Blackbeard even gave Shanks his signature
scars.

00:37:57.335 --> 00:38:02.465
It was ages and ages ago when we saw the series’
first meeting between Yonkou - when Shanks

00:38:02.465 --> 00:38:06.775
went to Whitebeard to warn him about Teach’s
machinations.

00:38:06.775 --> 00:38:12.675
I’m scared to even speak the words, so let’s
knock on wood as we say: Blackbeard might

00:38:12.675 --> 00:38:13.865
kill Shanks.

00:38:13.865 --> 00:38:19.214
He could even do so before Luffy is able to
reunite with him and return the straw hat.

00:38:19.214 --> 00:38:25.075
It would likely be the most emotional moment
in the series to date, but it would definitely

00:38:25.075 --> 00:38:32.175
make for the most satisfying smackdown in
manga history once Luffy took his revenge.

00:38:32.175 --> 00:38:33.765
**Luffy’s execution**

00:38:33.765 --> 00:38:36.025
A lot of classic tales are circular.

00:38:36.025 --> 00:38:40.985
They end where they began and a story can
have a beautiful poetry to it when the author

00:38:40.985 --> 00:38:43.435
uses this effect.

00:38:43.435 --> 00:38:47.474
One Piece opens with the execution of the
pirate king, Gol D. Roger.

00:38:47.474 --> 00:38:51.065
It could very well end with the execution
of the next pirate king.

00:38:51.065 --> 00:38:56.796
If Roger’s death urged a new generation
of pirates to set out to sea, Luffy’s could

00:38:56.796 --> 00:38:57.796
too.

00:38:57.796 --> 00:39:01.915
Luffy is the type of person who wants to see
everyone in the world taste the freedom and

00:39:01.915 --> 00:39:03.964
adventure of a life at sea.

00:39:03.964 --> 00:39:09.295
As bittersweet as Luffy’s death could be,
it could also make for a beautiful ending

00:39:09.295 --> 00:39:10.635
to the series.

00:39:10.635 --> 00:39:13.035
**Caribou Baroque Works**

00:39:13.035 --> 00:39:15.955
This is another theory by the YouTuber Randy
Troy.

00:39:15.955 --> 00:39:21.675
Caribou, the swampiest character in One Piece,
has stumbled face first into some huge information

00:39:21.675 --> 00:39:23.765
about the ancient weapons.

00:39:23.765 --> 00:39:27.964
Information that he’s hinted he wants to
bring to a certain someone.

00:39:27.964 --> 00:39:33.285
Prior to the Wano arc, it was thought he’d
trade this information to Big Mom or Kaidou,

00:39:33.285 --> 00:39:37.395
but with them out of the picture, we’re
running out of options.

00:39:37.395 --> 00:39:42.715
Teach is a prime candidate, but this theory
posits another major player in the New World:

00:39:42.715 --> 00:39:45.085
Sir Crocodile of the Cross Guild.

00:39:45.085 --> 00:39:49.155
The theory comes from the fact that Caribou
doesn’t look too far off from the concept

00:39:49.155 --> 00:39:50.444
art of Mr. 10.

00:39:50.444 --> 00:39:55.875
Mr. 10 was a Baroque Works member that was
mentioned by Vivi, but who we never actually

00:39:55.875 --> 00:39:57.235
met in the series.

00:39:57.235 --> 00:40:01.005
However, in Oda’s preliminary sketches of
the character, there are some similarities

00:40:01.005 --> 00:40:02.005
to Caribou.

00:40:02.005 --> 00:40:07.695
The face shape and generally wild hair are
pretty true to Caribou’s character design.

00:40:07.695 --> 00:40:12.055
Is it possible that Caribou has been a former
underling of Crocodile all along?

00:40:12.055 --> 00:40:16.185
After all, Crocodile’s initial goal in Alabasta
was to obtain the Ancient Weapon Pluton - and

00:40:16.185 --> 00:40:20.445
now Caribou could help him finally succeed
in that mission.

00:40:20.445 --> 00:40:21.474
**Emerald City**

00:40:21.474 --> 00:40:26.234
When the Straw Hats first encountered Bellamy
the Hyena, he laughed them off for believing

00:40:26.234 --> 00:40:30.035
in myths such as the City of Gold and the
One Piece.

00:40:30.035 --> 00:40:35.994
In his list of ludicrous dreams, though, he
also mentioned an Emerald City.

00:40:35.994 --> 00:40:39.675
The Straw Hats would soon encounter the City
of Gold in Skypiea and Whitebeard has taught

00:40:39.675 --> 00:40:41.935
us that the One Piece is Real.

00:40:41.935 --> 00:40:47.035
So, does Bellamy’s third entry, the Emerald
City, also exist?

00:40:47.035 --> 00:40:51.825
Who’s to say Oda doesn’t have time left
in the final saga to shoehorn in a quick Wizard

00:40:51.825 --> 00:40:53.785
of Oz inspired arc?

00:40:53.785 --> 00:40:55.925
**Lurking Legend Gin**

00:40:55.925 --> 00:41:02.025
At Jump Festa 2018, Oda hinted that a “Lurking
Legend” would appear in One Piece during

00:41:02.025 --> 00:41:03.085
the Wano arc.

00:41:03.085 --> 00:41:08.075
He also teased that this figure would be the
Straw Hats strongest opponent.

00:41:08.075 --> 00:41:11.855
For years, fans have theorized on who this
Lurking Legend could be.

00:41:11.855 --> 00:41:18.385
In fact, Wano came and went, and we’re still
not 100% clear on who the Lurking Legend was.

00:41:18.385 --> 00:41:22.485
The most likely candidates are Imu-Sama or
Rocks D. Xebec, however, the fan community

00:41:22.485 --> 00:41:25.795
has come up with some truly wild guesses.

00:41:25.795 --> 00:41:30.665
Among these are Shiki the Golden Lion and
other super-powerful figures.

00:41:30.665 --> 00:41:32.494
The wildest guess, though?

00:41:32.494 --> 00:41:37.795
Gin - the former crewmate of Don Krieg who
the Straw Hats encountered during the Baratie

00:41:37.795 --> 00:41:38.795
arc.

00:41:38.795 --> 00:41:43.665
After all, Gin promised to meet our crew again
one day in the New World…and we’ve been

00:41:43.665 --> 00:41:45.224
waiting ever since.

00:41:45.224 --> 00:41:46.224
**Tier 5**

00:41:46.224 --> 00:41:47.224
Woah.

00:41:47.224 --> 00:41:48.224
We’re halfway there.

00:41:48.224 --> 00:41:52.805
At this point we dare not leave our craft…at
least not if we don’t want to get the bends.

00:41:52.805 --> 00:41:58.714
At this depth of fandom, the pressure of the
depths could crush us - just as the depths

00:41:58.714 --> 00:42:04.214
of One Piece lore crush the minds of casual
fans.

00:42:04.214 --> 00:42:08.545
**Koushiro is Denjiro**

00:42:08.545 --> 00:42:12.565
Before we learned that Kyoshiro was actually
Denjiro after going through grudge-induced

00:42:12.565 --> 00:42:17.905
plastic surgery, many fans noticed that the
Denjiro in Oden’s flashback looked a whole

00:42:17.905 --> 00:42:19.115
lot like Koushiro.

00:42:19.115 --> 00:42:25.385
Hold on - let’s flip back 1000 chapters
and remind ourselves who Koushiro is…especially

00:42:25.385 --> 00:42:30.055
since that name is awfully similar to Kyoshiro
in the first place.

00:42:30.055 --> 00:42:36.345
Koushiro is this guy - Zoro’s swordsmanship
teacher and Kuina’s father back from Shimotsuki

00:42:36.345 --> 00:42:38.085
Village in the East Blue.

00:42:38.085 --> 00:42:43.885
And I can understand why people would have
thought that this was a candidate for Denjiro’s

00:42:43.885 --> 00:42:44.885
identity.

00:42:44.885 --> 00:42:49.535
I mean, just look at him - he clearly just
looks like an older Denjiro.

00:42:49.535 --> 00:42:54.965
And we know based on the Shimotsuki name that
Koushiro probably has some connection to Wano.

00:42:54.965 --> 00:43:01.325
But leave it to Oda to surprise us with a
man so angry his face changed forever.

00:43:01.325 --> 00:43:02.955
**Zoro Sharingan**

00:43:02.955 --> 00:43:07.135
Zoro’s eye has been closed since the timeskip.

00:43:07.135 --> 00:43:11.125
For some reason, he hasn’t been allowed
to wear a classic pirate eye patch, because

00:43:11.125 --> 00:43:15.395
Oda is saving the eye patch for a very special
character at some point.

00:43:15.395 --> 00:43:19.385
A lot of the fan base, though, presumably
people who have watched a lot of Naruto, think

00:43:19.385 --> 00:43:22.585
that this eye can’t just be injured.

00:43:22.585 --> 00:43:27.484
No - Zoro’s closed eye must be hiding an
amazing power-up.

00:43:27.484 --> 00:43:30.055
Maybe he has a weird ringed eye like Mihawk.

00:43:30.055 --> 00:43:36.275
Or maybe Zoro got so lost that he found himself
in the wrong series and ended up with a sharingan…or

00:43:36.275 --> 00:43:42.755
a rinnegan…or a byakugan…man Naruto has
a lot of different kinds of eyes.

00:43:42.755 --> 00:43:46.605
**The One Piece is destroying the Red Line**

00:43:46.605 --> 00:43:51.065
I don’t know about you, but as a long time
member of the fan community, the legendary

00:43:51.065 --> 00:43:56.855
Inherited Will theory is the first “mega-theory”
that I can remember reading.

00:43:56.855 --> 00:44:01.815
Many other super-sized theories have come
after -&nbsp; huge, sprawling monoliths dedicated

00:44:01.815 --> 00:44:05.255
to uncovering the greatest mysteries of the
series.

00:44:05.255 --> 00:44:06.255
What is the One Piece?

00:44:06.255 --> 00:44:08.244
What purpose do the ancient weapons serve?

00:44:08.244 --> 00:44:09.895
What is the Will of D?

00:44:09.895 --> 00:44:15.895
So many theories with mountains of evidence
have come, but one of the first, possibly

00:44:15.895 --> 00:44:21.765
*the* first comprehensive and believable theory
was the Inherited Will Theory posted on the

00:44:21.765 --> 00:44:23.125
Arlong Park Forums.

00:44:23.125 --> 00:44:27.665
If you’re unfamiliar, you should definitely
read the theory in depth or watch one of the

00:44:27.665 --> 00:44:32.065
many YouTube videos covering it, but a quick
version is this:The One Piece is destroying

00:44:32.065 --> 00:44:36.905
the Red Line, literally combining the seas
of the world into “One Piece.”

00:44:36.905 --> 00:44:40.345
It would likely take the power of the ancient
weapons to destroy this structure.

00:44:40.345 --> 00:44:44.994
It would mean the end of Mariejois, and thus
it would fulfill Madame Sharly’s prediction

00:44:44.994 --> 00:44:47.734
of destroying Fishman Island below it.

00:44:47.734 --> 00:44:52.085
And it would allow for many of the Straw Hats’
dreams to come true at once.

00:44:52.085 --> 00:44:55.694
Nami would be free to sail around the world
and map it.

00:44:55.694 --> 00:44:58.295
Combining the seas would create the All Blue
for Sanji.

00:44:58.295 --> 00:45:00.525
Brook would be reunited with Laboon.

00:45:00.525 --> 00:45:03.375
The list goes on.

00:45:03.375 --> 00:45:06.845
Having the theory in brief here does it a
disservice, so again, if you’re unfamiliar

00:45:06.845 --> 00:45:14.065
make sure to check out this theory.

00:45:14.065 --> 00:45:15.185
You won’t regret it.

00:45:15.185 --> 00:45:18.474
**People in snowy countries don’t sleep**

00:45:18.474 --> 00:45:23.444
On Drum Island, when Luffy is taking a sick
Nami to Dr. Kureha, he tells Sanji a rumor

00:45:23.444 --> 00:45:24.444
he heard once.

00:45:24.444 --> 00:45:30.244
He asks Sanji if he knew that people in snowy
countries don’t sleep - stating that if

00:45:30.244 --> 00:45:32.744
they do, they’ll die.

00:45:32.744 --> 00:45:37.855
Curiously enough, in a classic turn of Oda’s
god-tier foreshadowing, Drum Island was the

00:45:37.855 --> 00:45:40.895
first arc in which we heard of Blackbeard.

00:45:40.895 --> 00:45:46.325
Yes, we first saw Marshall D. Teach on Jaya,
but Dalton of Drum Kingdom states that their

00:45:46.325 --> 00:45:51.665
kingdom was attacked by the Blackbeard Pirates
which is why Wapol flees with his legion of

00:45:51.665 --> 00:45:54.055
doctors in the first place.

00:45:54.055 --> 00:45:58.925
Luffy probably heard the rumor about people
in snowy countries from Shanks, who knew Blackbeard

00:45:58.925 --> 00:46:00.204
as a child.

00:46:00.204 --> 00:46:05.755
Likely, the rumor isn’t about people from
winter islands, but about Blackbeard himself,

00:46:05.755 --> 00:46:07.825
who’s speculated to never sleep.

00:46:07.825 --> 00:46:11.585
A young Shanks and Buggy may have taken this
combined with the fact that Teach is from

00:46:11.585 --> 00:46:16.555
a Winter Island to concoct the rumor that
Luffy would repeat in Drum Island - setting

00:46:16.555 --> 00:46:19.935
us up for an eventual payoff when it came
to Blackbeard.

00:46:19.935 --> 00:46:25.704
**The D is a half moon**What could the D in
stand for?

00:46:25.704 --> 00:46:26.704
Gol D. Roger.

00:46:26.704 --> 00:46:27.704
Monkey D. Luffy.

00:46:27.704 --> 00:46:28.704
Jaguar D. Saul.

00:46:28.704 --> 00:46:32.335
All of these natural enemies of God have an
initial in common, but one theory suggests…what

00:46:32.335 --> 00:46:36.025
if this initial didn’t stand for a name
at all?

00:46:36.025 --> 00:46:41.204
Maybe it’s not Dream or Dawn or anything,
but it’s a pictogram.

00:46:41.204 --> 00:46:44.365
Maybe that D is actually a half moon.

00:46:44.365 --> 00:46:47.275
We know that moons are important in the series.

00:46:47.275 --> 00:46:48.484
Enel is chilling on one.

00:46:48.484 --> 00:46:52.325
The Celestial Dragons and winged races are
probably from one.

00:46:52.325 --> 00:46:56.265
The moon causes the minks’ sulong transformation.

00:46:56.265 --> 00:47:01.675
So it wouldn’t be that crazy for the D clan
to also have a connection to the ever-important

00:47:01.675 --> 00:47:03.505
moons of One Piece.&nbsp;

00:47:03.505 --> 00:47:07.665
Perhaps it’s so important to them that it’s
in their very name.

00:47:07.665 --> 00:47:09.295
**Sanji is dead**

00:47:09.295 --> 00:47:13.395
We’re not just talking about his fashion
sense after stepping through Vegapunk’s

00:47:13.395 --> 00:47:14.474
style changer.

00:47:14.474 --> 00:47:18.565
Back during the Zou arc, there was a ravenous,
bloodthirsty contingent of the fanbase who

00:47:18.565 --> 00:47:20.944
were convinced that Sanji was dead.

00:47:20.944 --> 00:47:25.135
Let’s look at the facts: Nami and the rest
of the crew didn’t want to talk about what

00:47:25.135 --> 00:47:29.625
had happened to Sanji, but he was clearly
absent during the arc.

00:47:29.625 --> 00:47:32.835
Then we found out that Sanji was wanted by
a Yonkou.

00:47:32.835 --> 00:47:36.724
And this was the first time we’d come face
to face with a yonkou.

00:47:36.724 --> 00:47:41.725
Big Mom, after all, in her first introduction,
was shown to be a cannibal.

00:47:41.725 --> 00:47:46.565
This was the early post time-skip and people
saw signs of a darker and harsher series.

00:47:46.565 --> 00:47:51.655
From the brutality of Doflamingo to seeming
willingness of Oda to kill off characters

00:47:51.655 --> 00:47:57.395
(compared to pre-timeskip) as evidence with
villains like Vergo and Monet, things were

00:47:57.395 --> 00:47:59.005
looking more violent.

00:47:59.005 --> 00:48:03.734
Some fans took this to mean that maybe he’d
turn the story upside down by having us lose

00:48:03.734 --> 00:48:05.555
a member of the crew.

00:48:05.555 --> 00:48:10.885
People also saw his Only Alive wanted poster
designation as a potential misdirection.

00:48:10.885 --> 00:48:15.234
Thankfully this theory was very wrong and
our shitty cook is still kicking.

00:48:15.234 --> 00:48:17.615
**Time Travel Training Montage**

00:48:17.615 --> 00:48:20.625
This theory belongs to the “Raid Will Fail”
family of theories.

00:48:20.625 --> 00:48:24.225
It’s very odd how little we know about Toki.

00:48:24.225 --> 00:48:29.595
We know she’s from the Void Century and
therefore is a well spring of important knowledge,

00:48:29.595 --> 00:48:34.905
and yet, after her sacrifice in Oden’s Castle,
we never hear from her again.

00:48:34.905 --> 00:48:39.575
However, since she flung the retainers forward
in time, it seemed that perhaps she had jumped

00:48:39.575 --> 00:48:42.305
forward in time as well.

00:48:42.305 --> 00:48:46.105
When things were at their most bleak for the
alliance in the war against Kaidou and Big

00:48:46.105 --> 00:48:51.845
Mom, this theory stated that Toki would appear
again and would once again fling our fighters

00:48:51.845 --> 00:48:56.045
to buy them more time to prepare against the
Yonkou.

00:48:56.045 --> 00:49:00.035
Luffy seemed out of his element, especially
before he unlocked advanced conqueror’s

00:49:00.035 --> 00:49:01.525
haki and Gear 5th.

00:49:01.525 --> 00:49:06.025
How could he possibly beat Kaidou without
more time to train and prepare?

00:49:06.025 --> 00:49:10.795
Well, by doing the same thing that Kinemon
and the others did, by going forward in time

00:49:10.795 --> 00:49:16.025
some undisclosed amount so that he could train
further and fight Kaidou another day.

00:49:16.025 --> 00:49:17.535
**Vegapunk Alien**

00:49:17.535 --> 00:49:22.395
Dr. Vegapunk has created the wildest technological
marvels of the One Piece world.

00:49:22.395 --> 00:49:28.075
He’s created artificial devil fruits, weather
control systems, the pacifista, and more.

00:49:28.075 --> 00:49:31.464
How could one scientific genius make so many
amazing inventions?

00:49:31.464 --> 00:49:32.464
Aliens [Show the ancient aliens guy].

00:49:32.464 --> 00:49:36.735
We already know that aliens in the form of
space pirates and possibly the winged races

00:49:36.735 --> 00:49:37.735
exist.

00:49:37.735 --> 00:49:43.675
So perhaps Vegapunk is a long lost member
of an advanced interstellar civilization introducing

00:49:43.675 --> 00:49:48.985
his peoples’ technologies to the Blue Sea.

00:49:48.985 --> 00:49:54.615
**Two Piece**

00:49:54.615 --> 00:49:56.585
What comes after the One Piece?

00:49:56.585 --> 00:49:58.145
The Two Piece, of course.

00:49:58.145 --> 00:50:03.025
This in-joke in the fandom states that after
the final chapter closes One Piece, Two Piece

00:50:03.025 --> 00:50:04.065
will begin serialization.

00:50:04.065 --> 00:50:08.415
After all, why would Shonen Jump let their
biggest property rest when they could keep

00:50:08.415 --> 00:50:12.005
making those sweet stacks of pirate cash.

00:50:12.005 --> 00:50:17.765
Just as Naruto was followed by Boruto, following
Naruto’s son, One Piece will be followed

00:50:17.765 --> 00:50:23.765
by Two Piece, then Three Piece, and so on,
and so on, until the inevitable heat death

00:50:23.765 --> 00:50:25.424
of the universe.

00:50:25.424 --> 00:50:27.815
**Sniper Island**

00:50:27.815 --> 00:50:29.365
Where is Sniper Island?

00:50:29.365 --> 00:50:32.684
If Sogeking is to be believed, it’s in your
heart.

00:50:32.684 --> 00:50:38.045
However, we all know that Usopp’s lies have
a tendency to come true, as explored on a

00:50:38.045 --> 00:50:40.494
previous tier of the iceberg.

00:50:40.494 --> 00:50:44.714
What if Sniper Island really is a place in
the Grand Line?

00:50:44.714 --> 00:50:49.365
What if there’s an actual Sniper King who
Usopp will either learn from or have to go

00:50:49.365 --> 00:50:50.535
toe-to-toe with?

00:50:50.535 --> 00:50:55.125
Listen, I know we’re expecting a giant sized
arc one day in Elbaf - after all, we’d love

00:50:55.125 --> 00:50:59.835
to get more closure on Big Mom’s story arc
as well as see what our favorite giants like

00:50:59.835 --> 00:51:04.955
Dorry, Brogy, and Hajrudin are all up to,
but perhaps it’s not Elbaf where Usopp will

00:51:04.955 --> 00:51:09.125
become a brave warrior of the sea, but Sniper
Island itself.

00:51:09.125 --> 00:51:11.105
**Carrot is the Traitor**

00:51:11.105 --> 00:51:14.945
In retrospect, it seemed obvious that Kanjuro
was the traitor.

00:51:14.945 --> 00:51:20.285
In Kabuki plays, after all, the artist archetype
is often cast as a villain or betrayer.

00:51:20.285 --> 00:51:23.974
His design itself was the biggest clue as
to his true allegiances.

00:51:23.974 --> 00:51:29.185
However, while we did know there was a traitor
- someone who was feeding information such

00:51:29.185 --> 00:51:33.835
as the whereabouts of Zou to the Beast Pirates
- that didn’t stop the fan community from

00:51:33.835 --> 00:51:36.474
making all kinds of guesses.

00:51:36.474 --> 00:51:37.655
One of the wildest?

00:51:37.655 --> 00:51:44.385
That Carrot - new leader of Zou and Straw
Hat in our hearts - was the traitor.

00:51:44.385 --> 00:51:47.724
She was sneaky enough to infiltrate the Thousand
Sunny, after all.

00:51:47.724 --> 00:51:54.505
And she was mysteriously absent from a lot
of the proceedings on Wano - suspicious much?

00:51:54.505 --> 00:52:00.075
Turns out, though, she wasn’t a spy - she
was just sort of…done being plot relevant.

00:52:00.075 --> 00:52:01.535
**TIER 6**

00:52:01.535 --> 00:52:04.545
I can’t remember what light looks like.

00:52:04.545 --> 00:52:09.214
I can’t remember my own name or the faces
of my family.

00:52:09.214 --> 00:52:16.835
At this depth, all there is is One Piece…*with
incredible enthusiasm* On to Tier 6!

00:52:16.835 --> 00:52:18.295
**Pell 9/11**

00:52:18.295 --> 00:52:19.655
Pell did 9/11.

00:52:19.655 --> 00:52:21.025
Wait, wrong notes.

00:52:21.025 --> 00:52:24.694
Pell is alive because of 9/11.

00:52:24.694 --> 00:52:29.645
At the end of Alabasta, Pell made the ultimate
sacrifice in saving everyone from Crocodile’s

00:52:29.645 --> 00:52:30.645
bomb.

00:52:30.645 --> 00:52:35.195
However, it just so happened that this chapter
came out right around the same time as the

00:52:35.195 --> 00:52:41.645
September 11, 2001 terrorist attack on the
Twin Towers in the United States.

00:52:41.645 --> 00:52:47.704
Rumor has it that Shonen Jump editors thought
it was in bad taste to have a character killed

00:52:47.704 --> 00:52:54.075
in a terrorist attack so close to this event,
and thus, the Will of P was born.

00:52:54.075 --> 00:52:56.425
**Kaidou in the Colosseum**

00:52:56.425 --> 00:53:00.895
In the D Block of the Corrida Colosseum, there
was a participant named Meadows.

00:53:00.895 --> 00:53:03.925
He wore a large leopard skin as a hood and
cape.

00:53:03.925 --> 00:53:07.335
He had a rather “beastly” appearance,
in fact.

00:53:07.335 --> 00:53:12.405
Since all we knew of Kaidou was that he was
the King of Beasts, one short lived theory

00:53:12.405 --> 00:53:17.625
was that this participant was in fact Kaidou
in disguise.

00:53:17.625 --> 00:53:22.615
After all, at that point, all we’d seen
of the Yonkou was a retconned silhouette that

00:53:22.615 --> 00:53:28.694
ended up looking nothing like Kaidou’s actual
appearance…but did share some similarities

00:53:28.694 --> 00:53:29.815
with Meadows.

00:53:29.815 --> 00:53:35.415
However, once Meadows and the rest of Block
D were taken out by Hakuba, this theory didn’t

00:53:35.415 --> 00:53:37.535
have a leg to stand on.

00:53:37.535 --> 00:53:43.415
Unless there were a few big Meadows stans
arguing that Cavendish was Yonkou level, of

00:53:43.415 --> 00:53:44.415
course.

00:53:44.415 --> 00:53:45.845
**Straw Hat Smoker**

00:53:45.845 --> 00:53:47.984
Who will be the next Straw Hat?

00:53:47.984 --> 00:53:51.045
It was a huge debate all throughout Wano.

00:53:51.045 --> 00:53:52.765
Would Carrot join the crew?

00:53:52.765 --> 00:53:56.585
Would Momo or Tama come along as a cabin boy
or girl?

00:53:56.585 --> 00:53:57.714
Would Yamato join?

00:53:57.714 --> 00:53:59.805
Well, Oda played us all.

00:53:59.805 --> 00:54:01.484
It was no one!

00:54:01.484 --> 00:54:06.835
I mean, we technically got Jinbe properly
joining the crew during Wano, but that was

00:54:06.835 --> 00:54:10.815
a foregone conclusion since way back in Fishman
Island.

00:54:10.815 --> 00:54:15.295
Though…we’re still wondering how he got
away from Whole Cake Island in one piece…

00:54:15.295 --> 00:54:19.224
Some theorists are looking forward to try
to predict who will join up next.

00:54:19.224 --> 00:54:25.615
And some guy [Show Mr. Morj] thinks that Smoker
will become a Straw Hat by the end of the

00:54:25.615 --> 00:54:26.615
series.

00:54:26.615 --> 00:54:30.755
The idea goes that Smoker joining the Straw
Hats would represent the ultimate merging

00:54:30.755 --> 00:54:37.195
between the Marines and the Straw Hats - Smoker’s
personal journey is all about finding justice…and

00:54:37.195 --> 00:54:41.625
this would mean he’d finally realize that
it’s not the World Government, but the Straw

00:54:41.625 --> 00:54:43.984
Hats that are truly on the side of justice.

00:54:43.984 --> 00:54:50.255
The question is: Will this man’s pride ever
allow him to call himself a pirate?

00:54:50.255 --> 00:54:51.714
**Charlotte Nami**

00:54:51.714 --> 00:54:55.845
Fun fact: We still don’t know who Nami’s
Mommy is.

00:54:55.845 --> 00:55:01.945
I mean, her real mom will always be Bellmere,
but her birth mom is unknown.

00:55:01.945 --> 00:55:07.045
And back in the first half of the series I
would have said it doesn’t even matter who

00:55:07.045 --> 00:55:08.045
Nami’s mom is.

00:55:08.045 --> 00:55:12.066
But let’s look at the facts: Luffy is the
son of the world’s most wanted man and the

00:55:12.066 --> 00:55:14.085
grandson of the hero of the marines.

00:55:14.085 --> 00:55:19.425
Zoro is definitely somehow related to the
former Daimyo of Ringo, Shimotsuki Ushimaru.

00:55:19.425 --> 00:55:22.755
Sanji is a literal prince of the Germa Kingdom.

00:55:22.755 --> 00:55:24.994
Usopp’s father is a member of a Yonkou crew.

00:55:24.994 --> 00:55:27.184
Are you starting to see a pattern?

00:55:27.184 --> 00:55:32.165
It’s not unlikely that Nami will follow
in the footsteps of the other East Blue crew

00:55:32.165 --> 00:55:35.955
members and have some kind of significant
lineage.

00:55:35.955 --> 00:55:37.895
But who is she related to?

00:55:37.895 --> 00:55:42.845
It’s almost certainly not Big Mom, but this
was a big theory back before and in the early

00:55:42.845 --> 00:55:44.984
days of the Whole Cake Island arc.

00:55:44.984 --> 00:55:47.184
But if not Big Mom, then who?

00:55:47.184 --> 00:55:51.275
Well, maybe we’ll find out in a later iceberg
entry.

00:55:51.275 --> 00:55:55.305
**The blond Gorosei is Sanji’s Dad**

00:55:55.305 --> 00:56:00.494
In my heart of hearts, part of me still wishes
this theory had turned out to be true.

00:56:00.494 --> 00:56:03.994
As soon as Sanji’s wanted poster at the
end of Dressrosa was revealed to have an Only

00:56:03.994 --> 00:56:09.635
Alive status, the gears were turning in the
community to figure out what was so special

00:56:09.635 --> 00:56:11.365
about Sanji.

00:56:11.365 --> 00:56:15.484
People had long thought he was important due
to little hints like his Mr. Prince identity,

00:56:15.484 --> 00:56:20.655
but now it was looking like our suspicions
were confirmed.

00:56:20.655 --> 00:56:22.535
The primary suspect?

00:56:22.535 --> 00:56:28.345
One of the Gorosei, the tall blond one with
the goatee, looks a hell of a lot like he

00:56:28.345 --> 00:56:30.615
could be related to Sanji.

00:56:30.615 --> 00:56:34.585
And as one of the highest powers in the world,
he definitely would have had the power to

00:56:34.585 --> 00:56:39.674
influence the wanted posters - after all,
we didn’t know about the Vinsmokes yet.

00:56:39.674 --> 00:56:44.575
And as much as we love our evil power rangers,
the Germa Kingdom, Judge…doesn’t really

00:56:44.575 --> 00:56:48.395
look like he’s related to Sanji other than
the blond hair.

00:56:48.395 --> 00:56:53.145
Hey, if the Gorosei are as old as we think
they are, maybe there’s still hope that

00:56:53.145 --> 00:56:59.085
the blond Gorosei is Sanji’s great great
great great great great grandpa!

00:56:59.085 --> 00:57:03.944
**Shakky was on the Rocks Crew**

00:57:03.944 --> 00:57:10.265
Our favorite Sabaody bartender and Rayleigh
life partner, Shakky, retired from piracy

00:57:10.265 --> 00:57:12.065
decades ago.

00:57:12.065 --> 00:57:16.974
However, we knew she was a major player in
the pirate world at some point.

00:57:16.974 --> 00:57:21.405
In the story’s detour to Amazon Lily after
Wano, we learned that she was actually the

00:57:21.405 --> 00:57:25.484
the former leader of the Kuja Pirates before
Boa Hancock.

00:57:25.484 --> 00:57:30.214
In retrospect, it makes perfect sense and
explains why Rayleigh has such a close knit

00:57:30.214 --> 00:57:33.075
relationship with the residents of Amazon
Lily.

00:57:33.075 --> 00:57:38.595
However, before this reveal, the prevailing
theory was that Shakky was actually a member

00:57:38.595 --> 00:57:40.395
of the Rocks pirates.

00:57:40.395 --> 00:57:44.875
After all, every other significant pirate
like Whitebeard, Big Mom, Kaidou, and Shiki

00:57:44.875 --> 00:57:49.174
were, so why not add one more member?

00:57:49.174 --> 00:57:54.225
Also, it would give Rayleigh and Shakky’s
romance a little bit of a “forbidden fruit”

00:57:54.225 --> 00:57:56.625
twist - a real Romeo and Juliet flair.

00:57:56.625 --> 00:58:02.135
But no, Amazon Lily it was, and we’re more
than satisfied with that reveal.

00:58:02.135 --> 00:58:04.964
**Celestial dragons are aliens**

00:58:04.964 --> 00:58:09.845
Let’s just look at the facts: #1: “Celestial”
has two definitions.

00:58:09.845 --> 00:58:14.885
It can mean “heavenly or mythical”, or
more literally, it can just mean space stuff

00:58:14.885 --> 00:58:20.234
- the sun, the moon, the stars - all of these
are “celestial bodies.”

00:58:20.234 --> 00:58:23.575
#2: These clowns wear space suits.

00:58:23.575 --> 00:58:26.995
And sure, they justify the giant fish bowls
on their heads by saying they don’t want

00:58:26.995 --> 00:58:29.225
to breathe the same air as commoners.

00:58:29.225 --> 00:58:33.734
However, that doesn’t change the fact that
the rest of their fashion looks very outer

00:58:33.734 --> 00:58:35.825
space chic.

00:58:35.825 --> 00:58:41.825
#3: As we’ve discussed on previous iceberg
entries already, we already have confirmed

00:58:41.825 --> 00:58:46.335
aliens in One Piece, so what’s a few more?

00:58:46.335 --> 00:58:48.145
The more the merrier, I say.

00:58:48.145 --> 00:58:49.145
Space Pirates?

00:58:49.145 --> 00:58:50.145
Skypieans?

00:58:50.145 --> 00:58:51.145
Lunarians?

00:58:51.145 --> 00:58:52.485
And the Dragons!

00:58:52.485 --> 00:58:55.244
**Oars was Joyboy**

00:58:55.244 --> 00:59:00.295
We may have already met the original Joyboy,
albeit in a roundabout way.

00:59:00.295 --> 00:59:05.005
Luffy seems to be Joyboy reincarnated - they
share a spirit, a dream, a soul, and even

00:59:05.005 --> 00:59:06.255
a devil fruit.

00:59:06.255 --> 00:59:10.224
However, they also may have shared a shadow
at one point.

00:59:10.224 --> 00:59:14.765
On Thriller Bark, the Straw Hat crew had a
tag-team fight against the massive zombie,

00:59:14.765 --> 00:59:18.085
Oars, a member of the Ancient Oni race.

00:59:18.085 --> 00:59:23.005
It would be all too fitting if the zombie
that received Luffy’s shadow from Moria,

00:59:23.005 --> 00:59:26.765
just so happened to be the previous incarnation
of Joyboy.

00:59:26.765 --> 00:59:31.505
We do know, after all, that the previous Joyboy
was likely a giant of some kind - the frozen

00:59:31.505 --> 00:59:35.085
straw hat beneath Mariejois is the biggest
clue for this.

00:59:35.085 --> 00:59:37.125
The biggest wrench in this idea is the timeline.

00:59:37.125 --> 00:59:41.954
The void century, around when Joyboy was purported
to live was 800 years before the current story,

00:59:41.954 --> 00:59:44.954
but Oars lived about 500 years ago.

00:59:44.954 --> 00:59:49.295
However, who knows how effective Moria’s
carbon dating is?

00:59:49.295 --> 00:59:53.414
With as much historical manipulation as the
World Government gets up to, this discrepancy

00:59:53.414 --> 00:59:56.155
could probably be brushed off by Oda.

00:59:56.155 --> 00:59:58.695
**Akainu is the leader of SWORD**

00:59:58.695 --> 01:00:04.974
Akainu is a despicable marine who has killed
innocent people and his fair share of Aces.

01:00:04.974 --> 01:00:07.855
Okay, well, one Ace.

01:00:07.855 --> 01:00:14.115
He is ruthless and will seek out any means
necessary to fulfill his idea of justice.

01:00:14.115 --> 01:00:18.595
SWORD is a secret organization within the
Marines that runs counter to the wishes of

01:00:18.595 --> 01:00:20.285
the World Government.

01:00:20.285 --> 01:00:24.315
Notable members include Koby, who actively
defied Akainu during the Paramount War and

01:00:24.315 --> 01:00:29.414
would have ended up thoroughly melted if it
weren’t for Shanks stepping in at the last

01:00:29.414 --> 01:00:30.914
second.

01:00:30.914 --> 01:00:35.765
Akainu and SWORD seem diametrically opposed.

01:00:35.765 --> 01:00:39.464
But have you considered this cover page that
shows Akainu shirtless?

01:00:39.464 --> 01:00:41.265
What is that tattoo on his shoulder?

01:00:41.265 --> 01:00:46.625
No, not the tribal one - his other shoulder:
That’s right, a SWORD.

01:00:46.625 --> 01:00:48.765
Therefore he must be the leader…of SWORD.

01:00:48.765 --> 01:00:56.474
Hey, I mean, a guy who takes care of bonsai
trees must have a secret soft side, right?

01:00:56.474 --> 01:00:58.674
**Shanks Haki Fruit**

01:00:58.674 --> 01:01:02.055
Shanks has never been seen to use a devil
fruit.

01:01:02.055 --> 01:01:06.234
In fact, there’s a very prominent scene
in Chapter 1 of Shanks swimming.

01:01:06.234 --> 01:01:12.194
Now, could he have theoretically eaten a fruit
in the meantime between Luffy’s backstory

01:01:12.194 --> 01:01:13.715
and the current story?

01:01:13.715 --> 01:01:18.085
Sure, but Shanks’ whole crew seems to be
made up of non-Haki users.

01:01:18.085 --> 01:01:22.635
Otherwise, it seems like we would have seen
at least one power so far.What we have seen

01:01:22.635 --> 01:01:26.674
Shanks make some crazy displays of is his
Haki.

01:01:26.674 --> 01:01:30.815
Arguably, he showed us Conqueror’s Haki
in the very first chapter when he scared off

01:01:30.815 --> 01:01:32.205
the Lord of the Coast.

01:01:32.205 --> 01:01:35.305
He also split the sky in his confrontation
with Whitebeard.

01:01:35.305 --> 01:01:41.265
But most recently, he forced Aramaki out of
his logia transformation and got him to back

01:01:41.265 --> 01:01:46.795
off of the Scabbards from miles away at sea
off the coast of Wano - and he did so with

01:01:46.795 --> 01:01:51.154
nothing but a long distance bolt of Conqueror’s
Haki.

01:01:51.154 --> 01:01:56.795
This is easily the wildest feat of Haki we’ve
seen in the series.

01:01:56.795 --> 01:02:02.325
For a long time, even before his awesome recent
feat, this crazy theory has speculated that

01:02:02.325 --> 01:02:08.974
Shanks’ use of Haki IS a devil fruit: that
Shanks is a Haki Man who ate the Haki-Haki

01:02:08.974 --> 01:02:09.974
no Mi.

01:02:09.974 --> 01:02:17.355
Granted, this theory was first conceived before
we had much understanding of Haki and is extremely

01:02:17.355 --> 01:02:18.355
unlikely.

01:02:18.355 --> 01:02:21.744
But did you click on an iceberg video to get
sane, rational theories?

01:02:21.744 --> 01:02:27.075
No, you’re here for the wildest stuff possible!

01:02:27.075 --> 01:02:31.494
**CP0 are Big Mom’s childhood friends**

01:02:31.494 --> 01:02:36.434
Big Mom’s backstory was one of the most
shocking and gruesome moments in the entire

01:02:36.434 --> 01:02:37.434
series.

01:02:37.434 --> 01:02:41.395
Sure, we’ve dealt with slavery, prejudice,
corrupt governments, and more.

01:02:41.395 --> 01:02:44.714
But one thing we never thought we’d see
in One Piece?

01:02:44.714 --> 01:02:45.714
Cannibalism.

01:02:45.714 --> 01:02:50.484
So imagine our surprise when we were treated
to Big Mom eating the worst birthday feast

01:02:50.484 --> 01:02:54.775
of all time in the form of all of her friends.

01:02:54.775 --> 01:02:58.904
But hear me out: What if…she didn’t eat
all of them?

01:02:58.904 --> 01:03:03.414
Eagle-eyed viewers noticed that a couple CP0
members who were present at the Raid on Onigashima

01:03:03.414 --> 01:03:09.215
somewhat resembled two of the orphans from
Mother Carmel’s orphanage who grew up alongside

01:03:09.215 --> 01:03:10.855
Charlotte Lin Lin.

01:03:10.855 --> 01:03:13.165
This theory seemed to make total sense.

01:03:13.165 --> 01:03:15.745
Firstly, the CP0 members all wear masks.

01:03:15.745 --> 01:03:22.115
When a character is masked, it seems logical
that they’re hiding their identity for some

01:03:22.115 --> 01:03:26.115
reason - as if it would be a big reveal when
they are unmasked.

01:03:26.115 --> 01:03:29.734
So some of us expected to know some of the
CP0 characters.

01:03:29.734 --> 01:03:34.605
After all, some other CP0 members turned out
to be familiar faces like Lucci and Kaku.

01:03:34.605 --> 01:03:39.555
It also makes sense because Mother Carmel
was known to sell orphans to the Marines,

01:03:39.555 --> 01:03:44.615
so if these two survived Big Mom’s birthday
party, it would make sense for them to end

01:03:44.615 --> 01:03:47.505
up as operatives for the World Government.

01:03:47.505 --> 01:03:52.405
And on top of it all, since Big Mom was present
at the raid, they could play perfectly into

01:03:52.405 --> 01:03:54.535
developing her story further.

01:03:54.535 --> 01:03:59.244
After all, we still haven’t had a chance
to see her reckon with the truth of her past,

01:03:59.244 --> 01:04:04.184
but we’ve seen flags foretelling it will
happen - such as her daughter Pudding having

01:04:04.184 --> 01:04:06.315
a memory fruit.

01:04:06.315 --> 01:04:11.684
Having left Wano, it seems like this theory
is dead in the water, but it will still live

01:04:11.684 --> 01:04:14.444
on in our head canon.

01:04:14.444 --> 01:04:15.444
**Done Piece**

01:04:15.444 --> 01:04:17.674
Done Piece…why does that sound familiar?

01:04:17.674 --> 01:04:20.714
Wait a minute, that’s a theory that I’m
known for!

01:04:20.714 --> 01:04:25.915
If you know my channel, you might have seen
“The Best One Piece Theory Ever, I Guess”

01:04:25.915 --> 01:04:29.405
- where I adapt this theory from Japanese
YouTuber Yuderon.

01:04:29.405 --> 01:04:34.515
Now, it takes a solid half hour to explain
fully, but here’s the gist: The original

01:04:34.515 --> 01:04:36.825
map of Jaya looks like a giant skull.

01:04:36.825 --> 01:04:40.895
The City of Gold in Skypiea was located in
the skull’s right eye.

01:04:40.895 --> 01:04:42.904
But its left eye is empty.

01:04:42.904 --> 01:04:43.904
The theory?

01:04:43.904 --> 01:04:49.904
The One Piece was this missing left eye and
currently resides…at the bottom of the strange

01:04:49.904 --> 01:04:53.845
hole beneath Enies Lobby.

01:04:53.845 --> 01:04:56.015
**Ancient Weapon Vivi**

01:04:56.015 --> 01:05:00.145
Crocodile’s master plan in Alabasta wasn’t
simply to take over the desert country.

01:05:00.145 --> 01:05:06.105
His actual ambition was to obtain one of the
Ancient Weapons, particularly the battleship,

01:05:06.105 --> 01:05:09.025
Pluton which was rumored to lay beneath the
country.

01:05:09.025 --> 01:05:15.025
Nowadays, we know that Pluton is actually
beneath Wano, but what if Alabasta was part

01:05:15.025 --> 01:05:17.404
of the puzzle of the Ancient Weapons.

01:05:17.404 --> 01:05:22.734
In fact, what if he had one of the Ancient
Weapons within arm’s reach all along?

01:05:22.734 --> 01:05:26.194
This theory states that Vivi herself is an
ancient weapon.

01:05:26.194 --> 01:05:30.924
It picked up steam after the Fishman Island
arc, when all of our previous notions of what

01:05:30.924 --> 01:05:35.924
an ancient weapon could be were shattered
when we found out that the mermaid princess,

01:05:35.924 --> 01:05:37.244
Shirahoshi, was Poseidon.

01:05:37.244 --> 01:05:41.984
Just as Shirahoshi can command the Sea Kings,
perhaps Vivi is also the conduit by which

01:05:41.984 --> 01:05:46.635
some force of nature - either Pluton or Uranus
is operated.

01:05:46.635 --> 01:05:52.964
In a dark twist, with Vivi now missing…could
Imu be using her as a key to utilize the destructive

01:05:52.964 --> 01:05:54.154
power of Uranus?

01:05:54.154 --> 01:05:55.494
**TIER 7**

01:05:55.494 --> 01:05:57.494
We’ve nearly reached the bottom.

01:05:57.494 --> 01:06:00.994
Down here there is only darkness.

01:06:00.994 --> 01:06:02.795
Darkness and One Piece theories.

01:06:02.795 --> 01:06:05.395
Oh, and those weird messed-up looking kind
of fish.

01:06:05.395 --> 01:06:08.066
But mostly just darkness and One Piece theories.

01:06:08.066 --> 01:06:09.095
Theories like…

01:06:09.095 --> 01:06:11.915
**One Piece is on the Moon**

01:06:11.915 --> 01:06:14.825
A large portion of the fanbase hopes that
much like Gamestock Stonks, the Straw Hats

01:06:14.825 --> 01:06:16.225
are going to the moon!

01:06:16.225 --> 01:06:21.885
Sure, Enel could come back to wreak havoc
on the Blue Sea, but surely Dr. Vegapunk has

01:06:21.885 --> 01:06:26.474
a spare spacecraft laying around Egghead Island.

01:06:26.474 --> 01:06:30.815
There are plenty of mysteries revolving around
the moon - some of which we already alluded

01:06:30.815 --> 01:06:35.605
to on a previous tier of the iceberg.

01:06:35.605 --> 01:06:39.755
What better way to explore the origin of the
Lunarians and the other winged races than

01:06:39.755 --> 01:06:41.595
to go straight to the source?

01:06:41.595 --> 01:06:47.505
After all, Laugh Tale is ludicrously hard
to reach - something has to be preventing

01:06:47.505 --> 01:06:50.605
sailors from just happening on it by chance.

01:06:50.605 --> 01:06:58.204
Sure, it could be terrible storms or something
- but how cool would it be if it were actually

01:06:58.204 --> 01:07:03.515
outer space itself preventing the average
pirate from reaching the One Piece?

01:07:03.515 --> 01:07:06.565
**Shichibukai 7 deadly sins**

01:07:06.565 --> 01:07:08.214
There are seven warlords.

01:07:08.214 --> 01:07:12.915
And ever since Fullmetal Alchemist named their
homunculi after the seven deadly sins, every

01:07:12.915 --> 01:07:18.065
group of characters featuring seven members
has been theorized as being representative

01:07:18.065 --> 01:07:19.345
of those sins.

01:07:19.345 --> 01:07:24.575
Unfortunately, while there are some good comparisons
within the group…the analogy kind of falls

01:07:24.575 --> 01:07:27.575
apart if you think about it for too long.

01:07:27.575 --> 01:07:32.575
The clearest analogues are probably Boa Hancock
as Lust and Gecko Moria as Sloth.

01:07:32.575 --> 01:07:37.235
Hancock because her powers rely on people
being infatuated with her and Moria because

01:07:37.235 --> 01:07:41.805
he gave up ambitions of traveling the New
World and traded them for building a zombie

01:07:41.805 --> 01:07:44.125
army to do his dirty work for him.

01:07:44.125 --> 01:07:50.035
Doflamingo and Crocodile could probably be
Pride and Greed…but what members of the

01:07:50.035 --> 01:07:52.855
Shichibukai *aren’t* prideful and greedy?

01:07:52.855 --> 01:07:54.595
I mean, they’re pirates.

01:07:54.595 --> 01:07:56.765
It kind of comes with the territory.

01:07:56.765 --> 01:07:59.984
Wrath and Envy are where things really fall
apart.

01:07:59.984 --> 01:08:04.085
Jinbe could *maybe* be wrathful because…he’s
angry sometimes?

01:08:04.085 --> 01:08:07.975
But really, he’s usually a pretty chill
dude.

01:08:07.975 --> 01:08:09.565
What is Kuma envious of?

01:08:09.565 --> 01:08:10.565
Having free will?

01:08:10.565 --> 01:08:11.565
Who knows?

01:08:11.565 --> 01:08:16.875
While it’s fun to speculate about, the Seven
Deadly Warlords just don’t really hold up

01:08:16.875 --> 01:08:18.015
to scrutiny?

01:08:18.015 --> 01:08:20.784
**Nami will control Uranus**

01:08:20.784 --> 01:08:23.404
Nami is One Piece’s #1 meteorologist.

01:08:23.404 --> 01:08:29.315
Thanks to tools like the Clima-Tact, the technology
of Weatheria, and now Big Mom’s homie Zeus,

01:08:29.315 --> 01:08:32.444
Nami has formidable weather-based powers.

01:08:32.444 --> 01:08:35.785
But how could they become even more powerful?

01:08:35.785 --> 01:08:38.635
What will Nami’s final upgrade be?

01:08:38.635 --> 01:08:42.674
According to this theory, it’ll be the Ancient
Weapon Uranus itself.

01:08:42.674 --> 01:08:49.574
Now, the only real evidence - if you can call
it that - is that Uranus is a God of the Sky

01:08:49.574 --> 01:08:52.705
and weather…also comes from the sky.

01:08:52.705 --> 01:08:58.625
Unfortunately for Nami, recent events would
suggest that it’s actually Imu who controls

01:08:58.625 --> 01:08:59.625
this powerful weapon.

01:08:59.625 --> 01:09:04.565
At least if that’s what we assume the giant
sky laser to be.

01:09:04.565 --> 01:09:08.134
**Christianity exists in One Piece**

01:09:08.134 --> 01:09:14.075
Sorry, Enel, but in One Piece there are plenty
of Gods ready to dethrone you.

01:09:14.075 --> 01:09:17.465
Obviously we have things like Sengoku’s
Golden Buddha fruit and Luffy being compared

01:09:17.465 --> 01:09:20.605
to the Wisdom King or the Sun God Nika.

01:09:20.605 --> 01:09:25.655
But apparently there are plenty of One Piece
characters who believe in and worship the

01:09:25.655 --> 01:09:27.495
Christian God?

01:09:27.495 --> 01:09:32.665
The implications of this have not been explored
in the story, but Kuma is clearly carrying

01:09:32.665 --> 01:09:35.215
around a Bible, the Christian holy book.

01:09:35.215 --> 01:09:40.315
We’ve also got the cultists who were trying
to worship Satan, but ended up with Brook

01:09:40.315 --> 01:09:41.315
instead.

01:09:41.315 --> 01:09:43.145
We have references like the Adam and Eve trees.

01:09:43.145 --> 01:09:48.135
And all of this begs the question: Is there
a One Piece Jesus?

01:09:48.135 --> 01:09:50.295
**Rocks is Imu**

01:09:50.295 --> 01:09:54.085
What if Rocks hadn’t been defeated at God
Valley?

01:09:54.085 --> 01:09:58.535
What if he actually did fulfill his goal of
conquering the world by reaching the Empty

01:09:58.535 --> 01:10:01.355
Throne and claiming it for himself?

01:10:01.355 --> 01:10:05.225
This theory was especially popularized by
Artur - The Library of Ohara’s fan comic

01:10:05.225 --> 01:10:10.665
the Return to Reverie, which explored an alternate
idea of what could have occurred after the

01:10:10.665 --> 01:10:11.665
Reverie arc.

01:10:11.665 --> 01:10:16.495
It sees Imu uncovering himself as Rocks and
doing battle against the Revolutionary Army.

01:10:16.495 --> 01:10:21.605
If you haven’t read it, I highly recommend
it because it’s super well made.

01:10:21.605 --> 01:10:25.215
It’s so professionally done that they look
like real chapters.

01:10:25.215 --> 01:10:26.945
**Fire Festival Ghosts**

01:10:26.945 --> 01:10:30.125
This one was a huge part of Joyboy Theories
Wano arc agenda.

01:10:30.125 --> 01:10:35.094
In Japan, the tradition of holding a fire
festival often connects to the idea of sending

01:10:35.094 --> 01:10:37.515
off spirits or reconnecting with ancestors.

01:10:37.515 --> 01:10:43.135
The thought was that the Fire Festival could
literally see ghosts of past characters manifest

01:10:43.135 --> 01:10:44.135
during the raid.

01:10:44.135 --> 01:10:49.245
At various points in the arc, characters impersonated
characters long thought dead.

01:10:49.245 --> 01:10:50.915
Kanjuro created a fake Oden.

01:10:50.915 --> 01:10:55.005
Black Maria created an illusion of Robin’s
mother and Professor Clover.

01:10:55.005 --> 01:11:01.225
This theory said that these characters and
more could come back to create some very emotional

01:11:01.225 --> 01:11:05.915
moments in which flashback characters could
see how much the Straw Hats have grown.

01:11:05.915 --> 01:11:10.505
And Oden appearing would have truly struck
fear into Kaidou.

01:11:10.505 --> 01:11:14.844
Add this to the list of theories that we’re
a little bit sad didn’t happen.

01:11:14.844 --> 01:11:16.645
**Snow bunny carrot**

01:11:16.645 --> 01:11:21.675
In Punk Hazard, we learned that when a devil
fruit user dies, the fruit reincarnates into

01:11:21.675 --> 01:11:23.835
a nearby piece of normal fruit.

01:11:23.835 --> 01:11:29.535
After Smiley the Doomsday Axolotl died, a
random nearby fruit turned into the Axolotl

01:11:29.535 --> 01:11:30.535
zoan.

01:11:30.535 --> 01:11:34.245
However, Smiley wasn’t the only devil fruit
user to die on Punk Hazard.

01:11:34.245 --> 01:11:36.985
Monet, the snow fruit user, also died.

01:11:36.985 --> 01:11:41.045
Now, we’re not sure about Punk Hazard’s
fruit reserves, but we do know that the Thousand

01:11:41.045 --> 01:11:46.145
Sunny happens to have a few of Nami’s orange
trees growing on it.

01:11:46.145 --> 01:11:50.505
The thought behind this theory was that Monet’s
snow logia would have jumped into one of these

01:11:50.505 --> 01:11:55.235
oranges to be unwittingly eaten by someone
on the Straw Hat ship.

01:11:55.235 --> 01:11:58.395
A prime suspect for this after Zou was none
other than Carrot.

01:11:58.395 --> 01:12:02.645
After the Sunny sailed away from Punk Hazard,
a strange panel featured a bunch of bunnies

01:12:02.645 --> 01:12:07.715
depicted in the waves beneath the ship, which
was thought to be foreshadowing of the Snow

01:12:07.715 --> 01:12:08.915
Bunny Carrot.

01:12:08.915 --> 01:12:10.514
**Evil Shanks**

01:12:10.514 --> 01:12:12.165
What if Shanks…but evil?

01:12:12.165 --> 01:12:17.345
Even though Shanks’s presence has loomed
over the series since the very first chapter,

01:12:17.345 --> 01:12:20.255
we know shockingly little about his actual
motivations.

01:12:20.255 --> 01:12:26.455
We know he’s wildly powerful - able to stop
the Paramount War with a single sentence - and

01:12:26.455 --> 01:12:29.885
we now know that he’s making his move to
claim the One Piece.

01:12:29.885 --> 01:12:33.715
We also know that he stole the Gomu Gomu no
Mi from the World Government…and might have

01:12:33.715 --> 01:12:36.955
known that it was much more than met the eye.

01:12:36.955 --> 01:12:41.755
We also know that he can seek an audience
with the Gorosei at his own whim.

01:12:41.755 --> 01:12:44.925
All of these details add up to make a super
mysterious character.

01:12:44.925 --> 01:12:48.485
And as Luffy’s hero, we’ve always thought
of him as a great man.

01:12:48.485 --> 01:12:52.875
But could there be a darker side to this emperor
of the sea?

01:12:52.875 --> 01:12:57.795
Could he be orchestrating events in the series
for his own purposes?

01:12:57.795 --> 01:13:00.465
**Seastone Sandals**

01:13:00.465 --> 01:13:06.165
The year is 2008.The arc is Sabaody archipelago.

01:13:06.165 --> 01:13:10.295
The One Piece fanbase would not yet know the
wonders of Haki.

01:13:10.295 --> 01:13:17.005
Logias were nigh unstoppable because of their
intangibility and there was seemingly no way

01:13:17.005 --> 01:13:20.265
to overcome them unless you had a natural
counter.

01:13:20.265 --> 01:13:24.955
The only ways we’d seen logias be defeated
before are when Luffy used water to defeat

01:13:24.955 --> 01:13:29.605
Crocodile and when he resisted Enel’s lightning
powers with his rubber body.

01:13:29.605 --> 01:13:31.525
However, there was one exception.

01:13:31.525 --> 01:13:32.525
Seastone.

01:13:32.525 --> 01:13:37.295
Smoker’s seastone Jutte had been seen to
incapacitate devil fruit users and seastone

01:13:37.295 --> 01:13:40.975
handcuffs or jail cells could keep them captive.

01:13:40.975 --> 01:13:48.045
So when we saw Dark King Rayleigh stop Kizaru,
a man made of light, with just a kick…the

01:13:48.045 --> 01:13:50.614
fan base jumped to some conclusions.

01:13:50.614 --> 01:13:56.935
Obviously the key to his stopping the Admiral
was in his footwear - his Kairoseki Sandals.

01:13:56.935 --> 01:13:58.695
**Pangea Kingdom**

01:13:58.695 --> 01:14:02.554
The base of operations for the world government
is in Pangea Castle.

01:14:02.554 --> 01:14:07.495
This idea states that Pangea Castle is actually
named for the Ancient Kingdom itself.

01:14:07.495 --> 01:14:11.995
After the kingdom fell, the World Government
took its place and took up residence in Pangea

01:14:11.995 --> 01:14:12.995
Castle.

01:14:12.995 --> 01:14:17.995
Moreover, Pangea Castle, which sits upon the
Red Line, is named for the super continent

01:14:17.995 --> 01:14:24.045
which once existed on Earth, before the tectonic
movement separated the world into the seven

01:14:24.045 --> 01:14:25.925
continents we know today.

01:14:25.925 --> 01:14:31.185
The theory goes that such a continent may
have existed in the One Piece world, before

01:14:31.185 --> 01:14:35.805
the world was separated into many islands
and scattered across the sea with the only

01:14:35.805 --> 01:14:38.985
continent remaining being the Red Line.

01:14:38.985 --> 01:14:39.985
**Mihawk Homie**

01:14:39.985 --> 01:14:44.195
In the beginning of the Whole Cake Island
arc, we received the revelation that Big Mom

01:14:44.195 --> 01:14:46.245
wielded the Soul Soul Fruit.

01:14:46.245 --> 01:14:50.575
This fruit filled her island to the brim with
all sorts of whimsical creatures who were

01:14:50.575 --> 01:14:57.205
imbued with part of her soul - the trees,
the food, and more were transformed into beings

01:14:57.205 --> 01:14:58.705
called homies.

01:14:58.705 --> 01:15:03.425
We also learned that as a tax for living in
Whole Cake Island, a small portion of each

01:15:03.425 --> 01:15:07.264
citizen’s soul was taken each year to empower
the emperor.

01:15:07.264 --> 01:15:11.665
When we learned about her soul manipulation
abilities, the community was abuzz trying

01:15:11.665 --> 01:15:14.435
to figure out the implications of this ability.

01:15:14.435 --> 01:15:20.514
Particularly, one homie named the Crane Rider
Randolph, a gallant rabbit warrior, made some

01:15:20.514 --> 01:15:21.705
viewers curious.

01:15:21.705 --> 01:15:27.235
They noticed some surface-level similarities
between Randolph and the warlord Dracule Mihawk

01:15:27.235 --> 01:15:33.435
and speculated that Randolph may have held
a portion of the Shichibukai’s soul.

01:15:33.435 --> 01:15:35.695
**Pandaman Guardian Angel**

01:15:35.695 --> 01:15:40.325
There is a special force watching over the
world of One Piece: the Pandaman.

01:15:40.325 --> 01:15:44.095
This Easter Egg character has been hidden
in tons of chapters all throughout the series

01:15:44.095 --> 01:15:46.014
- he’s practically omnipresent.

01:15:46.014 --> 01:15:52.875
It can’t be a mere coincidence that he’s
hiding in the panels of so many chapters,

01:15:52.875 --> 01:15:56.295
seemingly following the Straw Hats around
on their adventures.

01:15:56.295 --> 01:16:02.115
Perhaps he’s more than an Easter Egg and
this Panda-headed hero is actually the Straw

01:16:02.115 --> 01:16:03.745
Hats’ Guardian Angel.

01:16:03.745 --> 01:16:05.725
**Jango Power-Up**

01:16:05.725 --> 01:16:10.565
In Syrup Village, one member of the Kuro pirates
was Jango the hypnotist.

01:16:10.565 --> 01:16:15.225
At one point, he hypnotized members of his
own crew to increase their strength when they

01:16:15.225 --> 01:16:17.115
went up against the Straw Hats.

01:16:17.115 --> 01:16:22.475
However, as a gag, Luffy was also hypnotized
and started rampaging.

01:16:22.475 --> 01:16:28.135
This theory suggests that Luffy’s insane
strength throughout the series is all thanks

01:16:28.135 --> 01:16:29.785
to Jango’s hypnotism.

01:16:29.785 --> 01:16:33.074
In fact, Luffy is still hypnotized even now.

01:16:33.074 --> 01:16:37.085
It’s not just his will or his devil fruit
- he refuses to ever give up no matter how

01:16:37.085 --> 01:16:41.255
many times he’s beaten because he’s literally
compelled to do so.

01:16:41.255 --> 01:16:42.255
**TIER 8**

01:16:42.255 --> 01:16:43.255
Avast mateys.

01:16:43.255 --> 01:16:46.155
We’re finally here - 20,000 leagues under
the One Piece sea.

01:16:46.155 --> 01:16:48.885
I never thought we’d make it.

01:16:48.885 --> 01:16:53.105
The submarine is out of rations and I’m
afraid I’m not long for this world.

01:16:53.105 --> 01:16:58.345
But at least before I go, we get to explore
the most absurd One Piece theories of all

01:16:58.345 --> 01:17:00.614
time.

01:17:00.614 --> 01:17:04.625
**Kaidou is a Poneglyph**

01:17:04.625 --> 01:17:05.795
You heard me.

01:17:05.795 --> 01:17:06.935
Kaidou is a poneglyph.

01:17:06.935 --> 01:17:09.844
At least that’s what some people used to
think.

01:17:09.844 --> 01:17:14.055
All we knew about the fearsome Kaidou, the
world’s strongest creature, is that he was

01:17:14.055 --> 01:17:16.005
night indestructible.

01:17:16.005 --> 01:17:18.495
Nothing could harm this beast.

01:17:18.495 --> 01:17:19.905
You know what else is indestructible?

01:17:19.905 --> 01:17:20.905
Poneglyphs.

01:17:20.905 --> 01:17:28.094
Therefore, the only logical conclusion…is
that Kaidou was a poneglyph that ate the ancient

01:17:28.094 --> 01:17:29.585
oni fruit.

01:17:29.585 --> 01:17:31.415
**Devil Fruits are People**

01:17:31.415 --> 01:17:37.435
We’ve already had more cannibalism in One
Piece than in the average story (which…you

01:17:37.435 --> 01:17:40.175
know, not a high bar to cross, but still…).

01:17:40.175 --> 01:17:43.676
However, as we learn the secrets of the Ancient
Kingdom, it might be the case that One Piece

01:17:43.676 --> 01:17:46.185
gets a Soylent Green level twist.

01:17:46.185 --> 01:17:49.575
That’s right - Devil Fruits are made of
people.

01:17:49.575 --> 01:17:55.605
We’ve seen some possible evidence of past
users’ wills or memories or personalities

01:17:55.605 --> 01:17:57.225
being embedded into fruits.

01:17:57.225 --> 01:18:01.685
And it’s unclear whether fruits might impact
the users’ personalities.

01:18:01.685 --> 01:18:06.525
Is Luffy emblematic of freedom because he
ate the fruit, or did he eat the fruit because

01:18:06.525 --> 01:18:08.455
he’s emblematic of freedom?

01:18:08.455 --> 01:18:13.054
Same with Doflamingo being manipulative and
controlling and so-on and so-on.

01:18:13.054 --> 01:18:18.825
So, were devil fruits possibly created from
people who happened to have these abilities?

01:18:18.825 --> 01:18:23.605
And were their personalities or souls passed
along with them??

01:18:23.605 --> 01:18:26.265
**Imu D. Nami**

01:18:26.265 --> 01:18:29.915
As we discussed back when we talked about
Nami possibly being Big Mom’s child, this

01:18:29.915 --> 01:18:35.245
theory is also predicated on the idea that
we don’t know who Nami’s birth parents

01:18:35.245 --> 01:18:36.245
are.

01:18:36.245 --> 01:18:39.855
So let’s just get crazy with it: Nami is
Imu’s daughter.

01:18:39.855 --> 01:18:43.094
And let’s throw on the D initial just for
good measure.

01:18:43.094 --> 01:18:48.285
This would make for a Darth Vader level twist,
and hey, if she joins up with her pops, maybe

01:18:48.285 --> 01:18:51.375
he’ll let her control the ancient weapon
Uranus after all!

01:18:51.375 --> 01:18:56.784
It’s a win-win (other than the islands that
are obliterated off the map).

01:18:56.784 --> 01:18:59.045
**Sanji is Uranus**

01:18:59.045 --> 01:19:01.235
Okay, hear me out.

01:19:01.235 --> 01:19:05.665
Back in the day, minds were blown when we
found out that Shirahoshi was Poseidon.

01:19:05.665 --> 01:19:10.705
We had no idea that an ancient weapon being
a person was even a possibility.

01:19:10.705 --> 01:19:14.185
The mermaid princess is big, but she’s no
warship.

01:19:14.185 --> 01:19:18.235
So suddenly everything was on the table and
the fanbase was wracking our collective brain

01:19:18.235 --> 01:19:22.475
to figure out which characters could be other
ancient weapons.

01:19:22.475 --> 01:19:28.465
Conveniently, around this same time on Fishman
Island, Sanji had just revealed his Sky Walk

01:19:28.465 --> 01:19:29.465
ability.

01:19:29.465 --> 01:19:35.335
And Uranus is a God of the Sky…ergo…Sanji
is Uranus.

01:19:35.335 --> 01:19:38.165
Simple as that, really.

01:19:38.165 --> 01:19:39.824
**Kuina is Mihawk**

01:19:39.824 --> 01:19:41.515
Kuina is Tashigi?

01:19:41.515 --> 01:19:42.515
Broke.

01:19:42.515 --> 01:19:44.035
Kuina is Mihawk.

01:19:44.035 --> 01:19:45.395
Woke.

01:19:45.395 --> 01:19:50.425
Obviously Kuina didn’t fall down the stairs
- that would be such an unceremonious death.

01:19:50.425 --> 01:19:54.405
Clearly what actually happened is that Kuina
left with the Revolutionaries when Dragon

01:19:54.405 --> 01:19:57.665
docked at Shimotsuki when Zoro was still a
child.

01:19:57.665 --> 01:20:01.735
She was always told growing up that as a girl,
she could never become the world’s greatest

01:20:01.735 --> 01:20:02.735
swordsman.

01:20:02.735 --> 01:20:05.945
Therefore, she asked Ivankov to perform a
sex change on her.

01:20:05.945 --> 01:20:12.475
Afterward, taking on the new name Dracule
Mihawk, he became the world’s greatest swordsman.

01:20:12.475 --> 01:20:16.005
**The One Piece is in Barto’s Briefcase**

01:20:16.005 --> 01:20:21.534
In the Corrida Colosseum, when we first met
Bartolomeo, he was carrying a mysterious briefcase

01:20:21.534 --> 01:20:22.735
chained to his wrist.

01:20:22.735 --> 01:20:27.315
There was a panel that focused heavily on
this briefcase, suggesting that it was very

01:20:27.315 --> 01:20:28.315
important.

01:20:28.315 --> 01:20:31.645
The briefcase was never mentioned or seen
again.

01:20:31.645 --> 01:20:36.316
Obviously, we can logically conclude that
its contents were none other than the One

01:20:36.316 --> 01:20:37.316
Piece.

01:20:37.316 --> 01:20:41.605
Barto had found it in order to make an offering
to Luffy so that he could make his hero the

01:20:41.605 --> 01:20:43.054
king of the pirates.

01:20:43.054 --> 01:20:47.625
However, he was so starstruck when he met
the straw hats that he promptly forgot all

01:20:47.625 --> 01:20:50.975
about it and left the briefcase in Dressrosa.

01:20:50.975 --> 01:20:53.405
**Koby Final Boss**

01:20:53.405 --> 01:20:58.614
The first marine Luffy met on his journey
(not counting his childhood guardian, Garp)

01:20:58.614 --> 01:21:02.205
was Koby, the pink-haired cabin boy of the
Alvida pirates.

01:21:02.205 --> 01:21:07.375
Luffy has a dream to become the pirate king
and Koby has a dream to become a Marine Admiral.

01:21:07.375 --> 01:21:12.775
And while these two have been allies and friends
throughout the series, their two goals are

01:21:12.775 --> 01:21:13.775
diametrically opposed.

01:21:13.775 --> 01:21:18.735
A truly wild twist to the series would be
instead of Luffy going up against someone

01:21:18.735 --> 01:21:25.145
like Akainu, would be to go up against one
of his oldest friends in a clash of ideals.

01:21:25.145 --> 01:21:30.975
Koby would need one hell of a powerup to contend
with the future pirate king, but it would

01:21:30.975 --> 01:21:34.425
be a memorable ending for sure.

01:21:34.425 --> 01:21:37.545
**Big Mom NHC10 Addict**

01:21:37.545 --> 01:21:42.554
We all know that Big Mom has some serious
hunger pangs, but so do all the no-so-little

01:21:42.554 --> 01:21:44.895
kids that the crew rescue from Punk Hazard.

01:21:44.895 --> 01:21:48.935
That’s a pretty strange coincidence that
these seemingly unrelated characters both

01:21:48.935 --> 01:21:50.864
suffer from the same condition.

01:21:50.864 --> 01:21:54.885
However, there are a few connections between
them.

01:21:54.885 --> 01:21:58.885
Big Mom had contracted Caesar Clown to do
work for her and he was also the one who was

01:21:58.885 --> 01:22:02.075
performing gigantification experiments on
the children.

01:22:02.075 --> 01:22:06.295
The children’s hunger pangs and subsequent
terrible rampages were due to withdrawal from

01:22:06.295 --> 01:22:08.295
an addictive drug called NHC10.

01:22:08.295 --> 01:22:13.375
He fed this drug to the children by hiding
it in candies, much like the sweet treats

01:22:13.375 --> 01:22:15.825
that Big Mom often eats.

01:22:15.825 --> 01:22:20.695
Big Mom is also, notably, giant compared to
a normal human.

01:22:20.695 --> 01:22:24.325
Was she a failed experiment before being dropped
off on Elbaf?

01:22:24.325 --> 01:22:30.045
Is she, too, an NHC10 addict who is consistently
feeling some major withdrawal symptoms?

01:22:30.045 --> 01:22:31.915
**Oda is Pro-Monarchy**

01:22:31.915 --> 01:22:36.796
One would think that with story features like
the Revolutionary Army and Luffy’s general

01:22:36.796 --> 01:22:42.545
opposition to authority and declaring war
on the World Government, that Oda is very

01:22:42.545 --> 01:22:44.705
against authoritarian regimes.

01:22:44.705 --> 01:22:47.215
However, that’s not true at all.

01:22:47.215 --> 01:22:52.625
Oda seemingly loves kingdoms with one central
authority, a monarch, so long as they have

01:22:52.625 --> 01:22:55.715
a very nice king or queen instead of an evil
ruler.

01:22:55.715 --> 01:23:00.864
From Vivi, to Shirahoshi, to Rebecca, the
Straw Hats love their monarchs - it’s just

01:23:00.864 --> 01:23:06.275
when it’s a pirate or Wapol in charge that
this system of government really falls apart.

01:23:06.275 --> 01:23:08.425
**Rockstar is Rocks**

01:23:08.425 --> 01:23:14.905
Rocks D. Xebec was a scourge upon the One
Piece world, striking fear into the hearts

01:23:14.905 --> 01:23:17.755
of the World Government and other pirates
alike.

01:23:17.755 --> 01:23:21.605
Rockstar is a rookie who somehow landed a
spot on Shanks’ crew.

01:23:21.605 --> 01:23:26.855
Observant viewers will realize that the name
“Rockstar” has “Rocks” right in it.

01:23:26.855 --> 01:23:27.855
Coincidence?

01:23:27.855 --> 01:23:29.525
I think not.

01:23:29.525 --> 01:23:34.275
Is it not possible that Rocks did not die,
but simply waited and bided his time until

01:23:34.275 --> 01:23:36.645
his old rival Roger passed away?

01:23:36.645 --> 01:23:41.264
And since Shanks is very likely a Celestial
Dragon who was found on God Valley, he’s

01:23:41.264 --> 01:23:45.114
likely just waiting for his chance to take
out God Valley’s last survivor.

01:23:45.114 --> 01:23:49.835
**Zoro Bounty Hunter Long Con**

01:23:49.835 --> 01:23:53.344
When Luffy recruits Roronoa Zoro, the swordsman
laughs him off.

01:23:53.344 --> 01:23:56.385
After all, he was literally known as Pirate
Hunter Zoro.

01:23:56.385 --> 01:24:00.175
He was one of the most infamous bounty hunters
in the East Blue.

01:24:00.175 --> 01:24:05.735
This theory says that Zoro’s membership
in the crew is actually a long con.

01:24:05.735 --> 01:24:10.095
He may seem like the most unwaveringly loyal
crew mate.

01:24:10.095 --> 01:24:16.605
However, in actuality, he protects Luffy at
all costs because Luffy is his prey.

01:24:16.605 --> 01:24:19.535
After all, Luffy’s paltry bounty at the
beginning of the series is nothing.

01:24:19.535 --> 01:24:24.014
However, if Luffy can achieve his dream of
becoming the Pirate King, he’ll have the

01:24:24.014 --> 01:24:28.494
highest bounty ever known - and once Zoro
brings him into the marines, he’ll be set

01:24:28.494 --> 01:24:29.574
for life.

01:24:29.574 --> 01:24:31.344
**Void Century Bonney**

01:24:31.344 --> 01:24:36.755
Uh oh, this theory’s not looking too good
lately now that we’re in the Egghead Island

01:24:36.755 --> 01:24:37.755
arc.

01:24:37.755 --> 01:24:41.525
We’ve learned that in actuality, Bonney
is Kuma’s daughter and is learning about

01:24:41.525 --> 01:24:44.844
the Void Century along with the rest of the
Straw Hats from Vegapunk.

01:24:44.844 --> 01:24:49.425
However, just as it was once speculated that
she was related to Big Mom, her true age has

01:24:49.425 --> 01:24:51.244
always been a pressing question.

01:24:51.244 --> 01:24:57.105
If she can manipulate her age at will, it
seemed possible that she could be much, much

01:24:57.105 --> 01:24:58.585
older than she let on.

01:24:58.585 --> 01:25:03.085
Like…Void Century old, which could have
explained what Blackbeard wanted with her.

01:25:03.085 --> 01:25:08.815
However, now it seems that her preferred age
is simply her actual one.

01:25:08.815 --> 01:25:11.215
**Gaimon is the One Piece**

01:25:11.215 --> 01:25:15.494
I lied earlier when I said that One Piece
was the friends we made along the way or it

01:25:15.494 --> 01:25:20.565
was the Straw Hat or it was on the Moon or
in Bartolomeo’s Briefcase.

01:25:20.565 --> 01:25:25.965
Obviously the REAL One Piece is not the friends
we made along the way - it was one specific

01:25:25.965 --> 01:25:29.005
friend we made along the way: Gaimon.

01:25:29.005 --> 01:25:32.585
Think about it for more than a second and
it becomes obvious.

01:25:32.585 --> 01:25:35.635
First off - he’s on the Island of Rare Animals.

01:25:35.635 --> 01:25:36.905
What else is rare?

01:25:36.905 --> 01:25:38.445
The One Piece.

01:25:38.445 --> 01:25:40.225
Secondly - Gaimon is in what?

01:25:40.225 --> 01:25:41.824
A treasure chest.

01:25:41.824 --> 01:25:43.695
And what is the One Piece?

01:25:43.695 --> 01:25:45.364
A Treasure.

01:25:45.364 --> 01:25:49.364
Oda couldn’t have foreshadowed this revelation
any harder.

01:25:49.364 --> 01:25:50.905
Checkmate, theorists.

01:25:50.905 --> 01:25:51.905
**End**

01:25:51.905 --> 01:25:58.315
That was enough iceberg to sink Ten Titanic
Captains, but against all odds we made it

